/-!
# Stability under learning dynamics

Woodford (2003), *Interest and Prices*, Chapter 4, §2.3 "Stability under Learning Dynamics",
pp. 261–276, and Appendix C.7 (proof of Proposition 4.9), pp. 683–685.

## The general framework

* E-stability (`EStable`, `EStableAt`, `eStable_iff`, `eStableAt_affine_iff`), the T-map
  `Tmap` of (2.19) with its fixed points (`Tmap_fixed_iff_one_sub`, `Tmap_fixed_unique`), the
  rescaled time `tau` and the `2 × 2` eigenvalue tools are those of `Determinacy2Learning`
  (shared with Proposition 4.8). Here: the d.g.p. generated by a constant belief
  (`E_dgpMean_succ`) and that an s.c.e. is an r.e.e. when the disturbance is unforecastable
  (`sceMean_isREE`).
* (2.21)–(2.22): the recursive form of the sample mean of a random process
  (`sampleMean_succ_sub`, from `Determinacy2Learning.sampleMean_succ` path by path),
  `tendsto_tau_increment_zero` and the mean dynamics (`meanDynamics`, `meanDynamics_tau`).
  These are exact identities. The book's stochastic-approximation claims (that the mean
  dynamics approximate the ODE (2.20) and that beliefs converge almost surely, pp. 265–266) are
  results of Evans and Honkapohja (2001) that the book only cites; they are outside the scope of
  this formalisation.

## The Bullard–Mitra model under arbitrary expectations

* The model matrices are the canonical ones of `Determinacy2`: `B = taylorB`, `b = taylorb`,
  `A = taylorA` (C.19), `a = a25`, `Δ = taylorDelta`, the left side of (2.7) `taylorLHS`.
* (2.16)–(2.18): `temporaryEqm_iff` — under arbitrary subjective expectations, (2.16), (2.17)
  and the Taylor rule (1.14) hold iff `z = z̄ + B(Êz′ − z̄) + b u` with `u = r̂ⁿ − ī + π̄`
  (derived from `Determinacy2.taylor_pt`); `c19_iff`, `taylorB_mulVec_a25`.
* Spectral facts about `B`: `det_one_sub_taylorB`, `norm_lt_one_of_isEig_taylorB`,
  `determinate_taylorB_iff`, `not_determinate_of_not_taylor`. E-stability of `B` is
  Proposition 4.8 (`Determinacy2Learning.prop_4_8`), which is also the first block of the proof
  of Proposition 4.9.

## Regression learning (2.24)–(2.27) and Proposition 4.9

* `tMap`: the regression `T`-map (2.26)–(2.27); `E_dgp_succ`: the d.g.p. generated by any
  belief in the class is correctly described by a model in the class with coefficients
  `T(Φ̂)`; `dgp_succ_sub_E`: the residual is `(BΦ̂ₛ + b g′) e_{t+1}`, unforecastable.
* s.c.e. = r.e.e.: `sce_isREE` (every fixed point generates an r.e.e.), `sce_of_rational`
  and `sce_of_isREE` (beliefs whose forecasts are rational, or that generate an r.e.e., are
  fixed points; this direction needs the state to be non-degenerate and, for the second, `B`
  invertible), `affine_isREE_iff` and `fixed_of_ree_coeffs`/`ree_coeffs_of_fixed`
  (fixed points ↔ r.e.e. affine in the state).
* `fixed_existsUnique`: under (2.7) with stationary `C` the fixed point exists and is unique;
  `fixed_unique_bounded_ree`: it generates the unique bounded r.e.e. (p. 271).
* `tVec_eq`, `hasFDerivAt_tVec`: in vectorised coordinates `T` is affine with
  `DT = blockdiag(B, C′ ⊗ B)` ((C.28)–(C.29)).
* **Proposition 4.9** `prop_4_9`, `prop_4_9_at`: E-stable ⟺ (2.7). `taylor_of_eStable_dT` is
  the necessity half (error E28: p. 684 says "necessary for determinacy"; the argument shows
  necessity for E-stability). `not_determinate_of_not_taylor` confirms error E23 (p. 272
  "Not only is the r.e.e. determinate" should read "indeterminate").

## Phase diagrams, footnotes 38–39 and p. 268

* `piDot`, `xDot`: the intercept part of the learning ODE in deviations. Footnote 38:
  `taylorB00_gt_one_iff`, `piDot_pos`, `exists_piDot_neg`; footnote 39: `taylorB10_neg_iff`,
  `xDot_neg`, `exists_xDot_pos`; rotation of the loci: `piLocus_rotates_clockwise_phiPi`,
  `piLocus_rotates_clockwise_phiX`, `xLocus_rotates_counterclockwise_phiPi`,
  `xLocus_rotation_phiX` (counterclockwise only when `φ_π < β⁻¹`, imprecision recorded);
  `loci_coincide_iff` and `steadyStates_infinite_iff`, `fixed_infinite_of_eq`: at equality in
  (2.7) the loci coincide and there is a continuum of s.c.e. (p. 268, footnote 35).

## Preston's long-horizon forms (2.28)–(2.30)

* `forward_iff`: for `0 ≤ a < 1` and bounded processes, `z_t = E_t ∑ aᵏ w_{t+k}` for all `t`
  iff `z_t = a E_t z_{t+1} + E_t w_t` for all `t` (tower property). Hence
  `preston_IS_iff` ((2.29) ⟺ (2.17)) and `preston_AS_iff` ((2.30) ⟺ (2.16)) under rational
  expectations, for every `ExpectationSystem`; `preston_IS_not_imp`, `preston_IS_not_imp'`:
  the equivalence fails for general forecasting rules. `aggregate_demand` and
  `aggregate_inflation`: the exact linear aggregation of Preston's household spending rule
  (2.28) and price-setting rule over a probability space of agents with arbitrary linear
  subjective expectations, giving the aggregate-demand relation of p. 273 and (2.30).
  `sce_of_rational_needs_nondegenerate`: with redundant states (footnote 41) the converse
  s.c.e. ⇐ r.e.e. needs the non-degeneracy hypothesis. `gapIS_iff`: from the output form of
  aggregate demand (p. 273) to the gap form (2.29) — given that agents know current
  `Ŷ_t − g_t`, (2.29) holds iff forecasts of the natural-rate terms are consistent; this holds
  under rational expectations (`natSeries_rational`, `gapIS_of_rational`) and fails in general
  (`gapIS_counterexample`). Proposition 4.10 is deferred.
-/

namespace Woodford.NeoWicksellianFramework.Learning

open Matrix Filter Topology Determinacy2
open Determinacy2Learning (EStable EStableAt eStable_iff isEig_two_iff hasFDerivAt_affine
  eStableAt_affine_iff Tmap Tmap_fixed_iff_one_sub Tmap_fixed_unique tau tau_succ tendsto_tau
  prop_4_8 taylorA_mul_taylorB taylorB_mul_taylorA)
open BasicModel (xbar)
open scoped _root_.Kronecker

/-! ### The rational-expectations equilibrium relation -/

/-- Woodford (2003), the rational-expectations equilibrium relation of p. 268,
`z_t = z̄ + B(E_t z_{t+1} − z̄) + b u_t`, for every date and component. -/
def IsREE {ι Ω : Type*} [Fintype ι] (𝔼 : ExpectationSystem Ω) (zbar : ι → ℝ)
    (B : Matrix ι ι ℝ) (b : ι → ℝ) (u : ℕ → Ω → ℝ) (z : ℕ → ι → Ω → ℝ) : Prop :=
  ∀ t i, z t i = fun ω => zbar i + ∑ k, B i k * (𝔼.E t (z (t + 1) k) ω - zbar k) + b i * u t ω

/-! ### The sample-mean `T`-map (2.19) -/

namespace SampleMean

variable {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι]

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 264: the d.g.p. generated by a constant belief `zᵉ` through the
temporary equilibrium (2.18): `z_t = z̄ + B(zᵉ − z̄) + b u_t`. -/
def dgpMean {Ω : Type*} (zbar : ι → ℝ) (B : Matrix ι ι ℝ) (b : ι → ℝ) (u : ℕ → Ω → ℝ)
    (ze : ι → ℝ) (t : ℕ) (i : ι) : Ω → ℝ :=
  fun ω => zbar i + (B *ᵥ (ze - zbar)) i + b i * u t ω

/-- Woodford (2003), (2.19) p. 264: when the disturbance is unforecastable
(`E_t u_{t+1} = 0`, the i.i.d. case), the correct forecast of `z_{t+1}` under the d.g.p.
generated by the belief `zᵉ` is `T(zᵉ)`. -/
theorem E_dgpMean_succ {Ω : Type*} (𝔼 : ExpectationSystem Ω) (zbar : ι → ℝ)
    (B : Matrix ι ι ℝ) (b : ι → ℝ) {u : ℕ → Ω → ℝ} (hu : ∀ t, 𝔼.E t (u (t + 1)) = 0)
    (ze : ι → ℝ) (t : ℕ) (i : ι) :
    𝔼.E t (dgpMean zbar B b u ze (t + 1) i) = fun _ => Tmap B zbar ze i := by
  have h : dgpMean zbar B b u ze (t + 1) i =
      (fun _ => zbar i + (B *ᵥ (ze - zbar)) i) + b i • u (t + 1) := by
    funext ω; simp [dgpMean]
  rw [h, map_add, 𝔼.const, map_smul, hu t, smul_zero, add_zero]
  rfl

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 264: with an unforecastable disturbance, the d.g.p. generated by a
self-consistent belief is a rational-expectations equilibrium. -/
theorem sceMean_isREE {Ω : Type*} (𝔼 : ExpectationSystem Ω) (zbar : ι → ℝ)
    (B : Matrix ι ι ℝ) (b : ι → ℝ) {u : ℕ → Ω → ℝ} (hu : ∀ t, 𝔼.E t (u (t + 1)) = 0)
    {ze : ι → ℝ} (hfix : Tmap B zbar ze = ze) :
    IsREE 𝔼 zbar B b u (dgpMean zbar B b u ze) := by
  intro t i
  funext ω
  simp only [E_dgpMean_succ 𝔼 zbar B b hu, hfix, dgpMean, mulVec, dotProduct, Pi.sub_apply]

end SampleMean

/-! ### The recursive sample mean (2.21)–(2.22) -/

namespace RecursiveMean

variable {Ω : Type*}

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 265: the sample mean `zᵉ_t = t⁻¹ ∑_{k < t} z_k` of the observations
before date `t`, state by state (`Determinacy2Learning.sampleMean` applied pathwise). -/
noncomputable def sampleMean (z : ℕ → Ω → ℝ) (t : ℕ) : Ω → ℝ :=
  fun ω => Determinacy2Learning.sampleMean (fun k => z k ω) t

/-- Woodford (2003), (2.21) p. 265: the recursive form of the sample mean,
`zᵉ_{t+1} − zᵉ_t = (t + 1)⁻¹ (z_t − zᵉ_t)` (at every `t`, with `zᵉ_0 = 0`). -/
theorem sampleMean_succ_sub (z : ℕ → Ω → ℝ) (t : ℕ) :
    sampleMean z (t + 1) - sampleMean z t = ((t : ℝ) + 1)⁻¹ • (z t - sampleMean z t) := by
  funext ω
  exact Determinacy2Learning.sampleMean_succ (fun k => z k ω) t

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 265: the increments of `τ` become arbitrarily small. -/
theorem tendsto_tau_increment_zero :
    Tendsto (fun t => tau (t + 1) - tau t) atTop (𝓝 0) := by
  simp only [tau_succ]
  exact tendsto_one_div_add_atTop_nhds_zero_nat

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 265: the sample mean `zᵉ_{t+1}` uses only data dated `≤ t`, so it is
known at date `t` when `z` is adapted. -/
theorem E_sampleMean (𝔼 : ExpectationSystem Ω) {z : ℕ → Ω → ℝ} (hz : 𝔼.Adapted z) (s : ℕ) :
    𝔼.E s (sampleMean z (s + 1)) = sampleMean z (s + 1) := by
  have e : sampleMean z (s + 1) = ((s + 1 : ℕ) : ℝ)⁻¹ • ∑ k ∈ Finset.range (s + 1), z k := by
    funext ω
    simp [sampleMean, Determinacy2Learning.sampleMean, Finset.sum_apply]
  rw [e, map_smul, map_sum]
  congr 1
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun k hk => ?_
  have hks : k ≤ s := Nat.lt_succ_iff.mp (Finset.mem_range.mp hk)
  rw [← hz k, 𝔼.known hks]

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 265 (mean dynamics, first form): if at date `s = t − 1` the d.g.p.
implies `E_{t−1} z_t = T(zᵉ_t)`, then
`E_{t−1} [zᵉ_{t+1} − zᵉ_t] = (t + 1)⁻¹ (T(zᵉ_t) − zᵉ_t)`, here with `t = s + 1`. -/
theorem meanDynamics (𝔼 : ExpectationSystem Ω) {z : ℕ → Ω → ℝ} (hz : 𝔼.Adapted z) (s : ℕ)
    {Tz : Ω → ℝ} (hT : 𝔼.E s (z (s + 1)) = Tz) :
    𝔼.E s (sampleMean z (s + 2) - sampleMean z (s + 1)) =
      (tau (s + 2) - tau (s + 1)) • (Tz - sampleMean z (s + 1)) := by
  rw [sampleMean_succ_sub z (s + 1), map_smul, map_sub, hT, E_sampleMean 𝔼 hz s,
    tau_succ, one_div]

/-- Woodford (2003), (2.22) p. 265: the mean dynamics in rescaled time,
`E_{t−1} [(zᵉ_{t+1} − zᵉ_t)/(τ_{t+1} − τ_t)] = T(zᵉ_t) − zᵉ_t`, here with `t = s + 1`. -/
theorem meanDynamics_tau (𝔼 : ExpectationSystem Ω) {z : ℕ → Ω → ℝ} (hz : 𝔼.Adapted z)
    (s : ℕ) {Tz : Ω → ℝ} (hT : 𝔼.E s (z (s + 1)) = Tz) :
    𝔼.E s ((tau (s + 2) - tau (s + 1))⁻¹ • (sampleMean z (s + 2) - sampleMean z (s + 1))) =
      Tz - sampleMean z (s + 1) := by
  have hpos : tau (s + 2) - tau (s + 1) ≠ 0 := by
    rw [tau_succ]; positivity
  rw [map_smul, meanDynamics 𝔼 hz s hT, smul_smul, inv_mul_cancel₀ hpos, one_smul]

end RecursiveMean

/-! ### The Bullard–Mitra temporary equilibrium (2.16)–(2.18) -/

namespace BullardMitra

variable {β κ σ φπ φx : ℝ}

/-- Woodford (2003), (2.18) and (C.19): `b = −A⁻¹ a`, i.e. `B a = −b`. -/
theorem taylorB_mulVec_a25 (hd : taylorDelta σ κ φπ φx ≠ 0) :
    taylorB β σ κ φπ φx *ᵥ a25 σ = -taylorb σ κ φπ φx := by
  ext i
  fin_cases i <;> simp [taylorB, a25, taylorb, mulVec, dotProduct, Fin.sum_univ_two] <;>
    field_simp

/-- Woodford (2003), (C.19) p. 677 and (2.18) p. 263: the two forms of the rational-expectations
system agree: `e = A z + a u` iff `z = B e + b u` (here `e` stands for `E_t z_{t+1}`, all in
deviations from `z̄`). -/
theorem c19_iff (hβ : β ≠ 0) (hd : taylorDelta σ κ φπ φx ≠ 0) (z e : Fin 2 → ℝ) (u : ℝ) :
    e = taylorA β σ κ φπ φx *ᵥ z + u • a25 σ ↔
      z = taylorB β σ κ φπ φx *ᵥ e + u • taylorb σ κ φπ φx := by
  constructor
  · intro h
    rw [h, mulVec_add, mulVec_mulVec, taylorB_mul_taylorA hβ hd, one_mulVec, mulVec_smul,
      taylorB_mulVec_a25 hd, smul_neg, neg_add_cancel_right]
  · intro h
    rw [h, mulVec_add, mulVec_mulVec, taylorA_mul_taylorB hβ hd, one_mulVec, mulVec_smul,
      add_assoc, ← smul_add]
    have : taylorA β σ κ φπ φx *ᵥ taylorb σ κ φπ φx + a25 σ = 0 := by
      have h2 := congrArg (taylorA β σ κ φπ φx *ᵥ ·) (taylorB_mulVec_a25 (β := β) (φπ := φπ)
        (φx := φx) hd)
      simp only [mulVec_mulVec, taylorA_mul_taylorB hβ hd, one_mulVec, mulVec_neg] at h2
      rw [h2, add_neg_cancel]
    rw [this, smul_zero, add_zero]

/-- Woodford (2003), (2.16)–(2.18) p. 263: **temporary equilibrium under arbitrary
expectations**. Given subjective expectations `eπ = Ê_t π_{t+1}`, `ex = Ê_t x_{t+1}`, the
structural equations (2.16), (2.17) and the Taylor rule (1.14) hold iff
`z = z̄ + B(Êz′ − z̄) + b u` with `u = r̂ⁿ − ī + π̄` (the composite disturbance of (C.19); the
book's (2.18) writes `r̂ⁿ − ī`, absorbing `π̄`) and the interest rate obeys the rule. -/
theorem temporaryEqm_iff (hκ : κ ≠ 0) (hd : taylorDelta σ κ φπ φx ≠ 0)
    (infl x i eπ ex rn ib πbar : ℝ) :
    (infl = κ * x + β * eπ ∧ x = ex - σ * (i - eπ - rn) ∧
        i = ib + φπ * (infl - πbar) + φx * (x - xbar β κ πbar) / 4) ↔
      (infl = πbar + taylorB β σ κ φπ φx 0 0 * (eπ - πbar) +
          taylorB β σ κ φπ φx 0 1 * (ex - xbar β κ πbar) +
          taylorb σ κ φπ φx 0 * (rn - ib + πbar) ∧
        x = xbar β κ πbar + taylorB β σ κ φπ φx 1 0 * (eπ - πbar) +
          taylorB β σ κ φπ φx 1 1 * (ex - xbar β κ πbar) +
          taylorb σ κ φπ φx 1 * (rn - ib + πbar) ∧
        i = ib + φπ * (infl - πbar) + φx * (x - xbar β κ πbar) / 4) := by
  have hr := taylor_pt (σ := σ) (κ := κ) (φπ := φπ) (φx := φx) (kappa_mul_xbar hκ πbar) hd
    (p := infl) (x := x) (P := eπ) (X := ex) (rn := rn) (ib := ib)
    (r := ib + φπ * (infl - πbar) + φx / 4 * (x - xbar β κ πbar)) rfl
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨h1, h2, h3⟩
    have h3' : i = ib + φπ * (infl - πbar) + φx / 4 * (x - xbar β κ πbar) := by rw [h3]; ring
    rw [h3'] at h2
    obtain ⟨e1, e2⟩ := hr.mp ⟨h2, h1⟩
    exact ⟨by linarith, by linarith, h3⟩
  · rintro ⟨g1, g2, h3⟩
    have h3' : i = ib + φπ * (infl - πbar) + φx / 4 * (x - xbar β κ πbar) := by rw [h3]; ring
    obtain ⟨e1, e2⟩ := hr.mpr ⟨by linarith, by linarith⟩
    refine ⟨e2, ?_, h3⟩
    rw [h3']
    exact e1

end BullardMitra

/-! ### Spectral facts about `B` -/

namespace BullardMitra

variable {β κ σ φπ φx : ℝ}

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 266 and footnote 35: `det (I − B)` equals `1 − tr B + det B`. -/
theorem det_one_sub_taylorB :
    (1 - taylorB β σ κ φπ φx).det = 1 - tr2 (taylorB β σ κ φπ φx) + det2 (taylorB β σ κ φπ φx) := by
  rw [det_fin_two]
  simp [tr2, det2]
  ring

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 269 (proof of Prop. 4.3 via (C.19)): under the Taylor principle both
eigenvalues of `B` have modulus less than one. -/
theorem norm_lt_one_of_isEig_taylorB (hβ0 : 0 < β) (hβ1 : β < 1) (hκ : 0 < κ) (hσ : 0 < σ)
    (hπ : 0 ≤ φπ) (hx : 0 ≤ φx) (hT : 1 < taylorLHS β κ φπ φx) {μ : ℂ}
    (h : KroneckerSpectrum.IsEig ((taylorB β σ κ φπ φx).map Complex.ofReal) μ) : ‖μ‖ < 1 := by
  have hs := (schurStable_iff_roots _ _).mp ((taylorB_schurStable_iff hβ0 hβ1 hσ hκ hπ hx).mpr hT)
  rcases eq_root_of_eq ((isEig_two_iff _ μ).mp h) with h1 | h1
  · rw [h1]; exact hs.1
  · rw [h1]; exact hs.2

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 268 (and Prop. 4.3): the rational-expectations system
`y_t = B E_t y_{t+1} + w_t` is determinate iff the Taylor principle (2.7) holds, for every
`ExpectationSystem` with at least one state. -/
theorem determinate_taylorB_iff {Ω : Type*} [Nonempty Ω] (𝔼 : ExpectationSystem Ω)
    (hβ0 : 0 < β) (hβ1 : β < 1) (hκ : 0 < κ) (hσ : 0 < σ) (hπ : 0 ≤ φπ) (hx : 0 ≤ φx) :
    𝔼.Determinate (taylorB β σ κ φπ φx) ↔ 1 < taylorLHS β κ φπ φx := by
  rw [𝔼.determinate_iff, taylorB_schurStable_iff hβ0 hβ1 hσ hκ hπ hx]

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 272 (error E23): when the Taylor principle is not satisfied the r.e.e.
is **indeterminate**, so the printed "Not only is the r.e.e. determinate" is false; it should
read "indeterminate". -/
theorem not_determinate_of_not_taylor {Ω : Type*} [Nonempty Ω] (𝔼 : ExpectationSystem Ω)
    (hβ0 : 0 < β) (hβ1 : β < 1) (hκ : 0 < κ) (hσ : 0 < σ) (hπ : 0 ≤ φπ) (hx : 0 ≤ φx)
    (hT : ¬ 1 < taylorLHS β κ φπ φx) : ¬ 𝔼.Determinate (taylorB β σ κ φπ φx) := by
  rw [determinate_taylorB_iff 𝔼 hβ0 hβ1 hκ hσ hπ hx]
  exact hT

end BullardMitra

/-! ### Regression learning (2.24)–(2.27) -/

namespace Regression

variable {ι S Ω : Type*} [Fintype ι] [Fintype S]

/-- Woodford (2003), (2.25) p. 270: a forecasting model `z_{t+1} = Φ₀ + Φₛ s_t + ε_{t+1}`,
given by the intercepts `Φ₀` and the slope matrix `Φₛ`. -/
abbrev Belief (ι S : Type*) := (ι → ℝ) × Matrix ι S ℝ

/-- Woodford (2003), (2.26)–(2.27) pp. 270–271: the regression `T`-map
`Φ₀ = z̄ + B(Φ̂₀ − z̄)`, `Φₛ = (B Φ̂ₛ + b g′) C`, where `u_t = g′ s_t` is the composite
disturbance `r̂ⁿ_t − ī_t + π̄` (the book's `[1 −1] f′ s_t`). -/
def tMap (zbar : ι → ℝ) (B : Matrix ι ι ℝ) (b : ι → ℝ) (g : S → ℝ) (C : Matrix S S ℝ)
    (Φ : Belief ι S) : Belief ι S :=
  (zbar + B *ᵥ (Φ.1 - zbar), (B * Φ.2 + vecMulVec b g) * C)

/-- Woodford (2003), (2.25) p. 270: the random variable `c + a′ x`, affine in the state. -/
def affRV (c : ℝ) (a : S → ℝ) (x : S → Ω → ℝ) : Ω → ℝ := fun ω => c + ∑ j, a j * x j ω

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 270: the subjective forecast `Ê_t z_{t+1} = Φ₀ + Φₛ s_t` of component
`i`. -/
def forecast (Φ : Belief ι S) (s : ℕ → S → Ω → ℝ) (t : ℕ) (i : ι) : Ω → ℝ :=
  affRV (Φ.1 i) (Φ.2 i) (s t)

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 270: the composite disturbance `u_t = g′ s_t`. -/
def dist (g : S → ℝ) (s : ℕ → S → Ω → ℝ) (t : ℕ) : Ω → ℝ := fun ω => ∑ j, g j * s t j ω

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 270: the d.g.p. generated by belief in the model `Φ̂`, through the
temporary equilibrium (2.18): `z_t = z̄ + B(Φ̂₀ + Φ̂ₛ s_t − z̄) + b u_t`. -/
def dgp (zbar : ι → ℝ) (B : Matrix ι ι ℝ) (b : ι → ℝ) (g : S → ℝ) (Φ : Belief ι S)
    (s : ℕ → S → Ω → ℝ) (t : ℕ) (i : ι) : Ω → ℝ :=
  fun ω => zbar i + ∑ k, B i k * (forecast Φ s t k ω - zbar k) + b i * dist g s t ω

/-- Woodford (2003), (2.24) p. 270: the exogenous state follows `s_{t+1} = C s_t + e_{t+1}`
with `s` adapted and innovations unforecastable, `E_t e_{t+1} = 0`. -/
def StateLaw (𝔼 : ExpectationSystem Ω) (C : Matrix S S ℝ) (s e : ℕ → S → Ω → ℝ) : Prop :=
  (∀ t j, 𝔼.E t (s t j) = s t j) ∧
    (∀ t j, s (t + 1) j = (fun ω => ∑ k, C j k * s t k ω) + e (t + 1) j) ∧
    (∀ t j, 𝔼.E t (e (t + 1) j) = 0)

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 270: an affine random variable as a linear combination. -/
theorem affRV_eq (c : ℝ) (a : S → ℝ) (x : S → Ω → ℝ) :
    affRV c a x = (fun _ => c) + ∑ j, a j • x j := by
  funext ω
  simp [affRV, Finset.sum_apply]

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 270: an affine function of variables known at `t` is known at `t`. -/
theorem E_affRV_of_known (𝔼 : ExpectationSystem Ω) {t : ℕ} (c : ℝ) (a : S → ℝ)
    {x : S → Ω → ℝ} (hx : ∀ j, 𝔼.E t (x j) = x j) : 𝔼.E t (affRV c a x) = affRV c a x := by
  rw [affRV_eq, map_add, 𝔼.const, map_sum]
  simp_rw [map_smul, hx]

/-- Woodford (2003), (2.24) p. 270: the conditional forecast of the state, `E_t s_{t+1} = C s_t`. -/
theorem E_state_succ {𝔼 : ExpectationSystem Ω} {C : Matrix S S ℝ} {s e : ℕ → S → Ω → ℝ}
    (h : StateLaw 𝔼 C s e) (t : ℕ) (j : S) :
    𝔼.E t (s (t + 1) j) = fun ω => ∑ k, C j k * s t k ω := by
  rw [h.2.1 t j, map_add, h.2.2 t j, add_zero]
  have : (fun ω => ∑ k, C j k * s t k ω) = ∑ k, C j k • s t k := by
    funext ω; simp [Finset.sum_apply]
  rw [this, map_sum]
  simp_rw [map_smul, h.1 t]

/-- Woodford (2003), (2.26)–(2.27): `E_t (c + a′ s_{t+1}) = c + (a′ C) s_t`. -/
theorem E_affRV_succ {𝔼 : ExpectationSystem Ω} {C : Matrix S S ℝ} {s e : ℕ → S → Ω → ℝ}
    (h : StateLaw 𝔼 C s e) (t : ℕ) (c : ℝ) (a : S → ℝ) :
    𝔼.E t (affRV c a (s (t + 1))) = affRV c (a ᵥ* C) (s t) := by
  rw [affRV_eq, map_add, 𝔼.const, map_sum]
  simp_rw [map_smul, E_state_succ h t]
  funext ω
  simp only [Pi.add_apply, Finset.sum_apply, Pi.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul, affRV, vecMul,
    dotProduct, Finset.mul_sum, Finset.sum_mul]
  rw [Finset.sum_comm]
  congr 1
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun k _ => Finset.sum_congr rfl fun j _ => ?_
  ring

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 270: the d.g.p. is affine in the state, with intercept `z̄ + B(Φ̂₀ − z̄)`
and slopes `B Φ̂ₛ + b g′`. -/
theorem dgp_eq (zbar : ι → ℝ) (B : Matrix ι ι ℝ) (b : ι → ℝ) (g : S → ℝ) (Φ : Belief ι S)
    (s : ℕ → S → Ω → ℝ) (t : ℕ) (i : ι) :
    dgp zbar B b g Φ s t i =
      affRV (zbar i + (B *ᵥ (Φ.1 - zbar)) i) ((B * Φ.2 + vecMulVec b g) i) (s t) := by
  funext ω
  simp only [dgp, forecast, affRV, dist, mulVec, dotProduct, Pi.sub_apply, Matrix.add_apply,
    Matrix.mul_apply, vecMulVec_apply, add_mul, Finset.sum_add_distrib, Finset.sum_mul,
    Finset.mul_sum]
  rw [Finset.sum_comm (f := fun x y => B i y * Φ.2 y x * s t x ω)]
  have h1 : ∀ k, B i k * (Φ.1 k + ∑ j, Φ.2 k j * s t j ω - zbar k) =
      B i k * (Φ.1 k - zbar k) + ∑ j, B i k * Φ.2 k j * s t j ω := by
    intro k
    rw [show Φ.1 k + ∑ j, Φ.2 k j * s t j ω - zbar k =
      (Φ.1 k - zbar k) + ∑ j, Φ.2 k j * s t j ω by ring, mul_add, Finset.mul_sum]
    simp only [mul_assoc]
  simp only [h1, Finset.sum_add_distrib]
  ring_nf

/-- Woodford (2003), (2.26)–(2.27) pp. 270–271: belief in the model `Φ̂` generates data whose
correct forecast is the model `T(Φ̂)` in the same class: `E_t z_{t+1} = T(Φ̂)₀ + T(Φ̂)ₛ s_t`. -/
theorem E_dgp_succ {𝔼 : ExpectationSystem Ω} {C : Matrix S S ℝ} {s e : ℕ → S → Ω → ℝ}
    (h : StateLaw 𝔼 C s e) (zbar : ι → ℝ) (B : Matrix ι ι ℝ) (b : ι → ℝ) (g : S → ℝ)
    (Φ : Belief ι S) (t : ℕ) (i : ι) :
    𝔼.E t (dgp zbar B b g Φ s (t + 1) i) = forecast (tMap zbar B b g C Φ) s t i := by
  rw [dgp_eq, E_affRV_succ h]
  rfl

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 271: the forecast error of the correct model is
`z_{t+1} − E_t z_{t+1} = (B Φ̂ₛ + b g′) e_{t+1}`. -/
theorem dgp_succ_sub_E {𝔼 : ExpectationSystem Ω} {C : Matrix S S ℝ} {s e : ℕ → S → Ω → ℝ}
    (h : StateLaw 𝔼 C s e) (zbar : ι → ℝ) (B : Matrix ι ι ℝ) (b : ι → ℝ) (g : S → ℝ)
    (Φ : Belief ι S) (t : ℕ) (i : ι) :
    dgp zbar B b g Φ s (t + 1) i - 𝔼.E t (dgp zbar B b g Φ s (t + 1) i) =
      fun ω => ∑ j, (B * Φ.2 + vecMulVec b g) i j * e (t + 1) j ω := by
  rw [E_dgp_succ h, dgp_eq]
  funext ω
  simp only [Pi.sub_apply, affRV, forecast, tMap]
  have hs : ∀ j, s (t + 1) j ω = ∑ k, C j k * s t k ω + e (t + 1) j ω := fun j => by
    have := congrFun (h.2.1 t j) ω
    simpa using this
  simp only [hs, mul_add, Finset.sum_add_distrib, Finset.mul_sum]
  have : ∑ j, ∑ k, (B * Φ.2 + vecMulVec b g) i j * (C j k * s t k ω) =
      ∑ k, ((B * Φ.2 + vecMulVec b g) * C) i k * s t k ω := by
    rw [Finset.sum_comm]
    refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun k _ => ?_
    rw [Matrix.mul_apply, Finset.sum_mul]
    refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun j _ => ?_
    ring
  rw [this]
  simp only [Pi.add_apply]
  ring

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 271: the residual of the correct model is unforecastable,
`E_t ε_{t+1} = 0`. -/
theorem E_residual (𝔼 : ExpectationSystem Ω) (s : ℕ → S → Ω → ℝ) (zbar : ι → ℝ)
    (B : Matrix ι ι ℝ) (b : ι → ℝ) (g : S → ℝ) (Φ : Belief ι S) (t : ℕ) (i : ι) :
    𝔼.E t (dgp zbar B b g Φ s (t + 1) i - 𝔼.E t (dgp zbar B b g Φ s (t + 1) i)) = 0 := by
  rw [map_sub, 𝔼.E_E_self, sub_self]

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 271: "a self-confirming equilibrium is actually a rational-expectations
equilibrium": if `T(Φ̂) = Φ̂`, the d.g.p. generated by `Φ̂` satisfies the r.e.e. relation. -/
theorem sce_isREE {𝔼 : ExpectationSystem Ω} {C : Matrix S S ℝ} {s e : ℕ → S → Ω → ℝ}
    (h : StateLaw 𝔼 C s e) (zbar : ι → ℝ) (B : Matrix ι ι ℝ) (b : ι → ℝ) (g : S → ℝ)
    {Φ : Belief ι S} (hfix : tMap zbar B b g C Φ = Φ) :
    IsREE 𝔼 zbar B b (dist g s) (dgp zbar B b g Φ s) := by
  intro t i
  simp_rw [E_dgp_succ h, hfix]
  rfl

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 270: the state is non-degenerate (no exact affine relation among the
constant and the state variables holds at every date and state), so that coefficients of an
affine forecast are identified. Redundant states such as an identically zero component violate
it. -/
def Nondegenerate (s : ℕ → S → Ω → ℝ) : Prop :=
  ∀ (c : ℝ) (a : S → ℝ), (∀ t ω, c + ∑ j, a j * s t j ω = 0) → c = 0 ∧ a = 0

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 270: under non-degeneracy, affine forecasts that agree at every date
have the same coefficients. -/
theorem affRV_inj {s : ℕ → S → Ω → ℝ} (hs : Nondegenerate s) {c c' : ℝ} {a a' : S → ℝ}
    (h : ∀ t, affRV c a (s t) = affRV c' a' (s t)) : c = c' ∧ a = a' := by
  have := hs (c - c') (a - a') (fun t ω => by
    have h1 := congrFun (h t) ω
    simp only [affRV] at h1
    simp only [Pi.sub_apply, sub_mul, Finset.sum_sub_distrib]
    linarith)
  exact ⟨sub_eq_zero.mp this.1, sub_eq_zero.mp this.2⟩

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 271 (converse direction, s.c.e. = r.e.e.): a belief whose forecasts
coincide with the true conditional expectations of the data it generates is a fixed point of
`T` (given a non-degenerate state). -/
theorem sce_of_rational {𝔼 : ExpectationSystem Ω} {C : Matrix S S ℝ} {s e : ℕ → S → Ω → ℝ}
    (h : StateLaw 𝔼 C s e) (hs : Nondegenerate s) (zbar : ι → ℝ) (B : Matrix ι ι ℝ)
    (b : ι → ℝ) (g : S → ℝ) {Φ : Belief ι S}
    (hrat : ∀ t i, forecast Φ s t i = 𝔼.E t (dgp zbar B b g Φ s (t + 1) i)) :
    tMap zbar B b g C Φ = Φ := by
  have key : ∀ i, (tMap zbar B b g C Φ).1 i = Φ.1 i ∧ (tMap zbar B b g C Φ).2 i = Φ.2 i := by
    intro i
    refine affRV_inj hs fun t => ?_
    have := hrat t i
    rw [E_dgp_succ h] at this
    exact this.symm
  ext i
  · exact (key i).1
  · exact congrFun (key i).2 _

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 271 (converse direction, s.c.e. = r.e.e.): if `B` is invertible and the
state is non-degenerate, a belief whose d.g.p. is a rational-expectations equilibrium is a fixed
point of `T`. -/
theorem sce_of_isREE [DecidableEq ι] {𝔼 : ExpectationSystem Ω} {C : Matrix S S ℝ}
    {s e : ℕ → S → Ω → ℝ} (h : StateLaw 𝔼 C s e) (hs : Nondegenerate s) (zbar : ι → ℝ)
    {B : Matrix ι ι ℝ} (hB : B.det ≠ 0) (b : ι → ℝ) (g : S → ℝ) {Φ : Belief ι S}
    (hree : IsREE 𝔼 zbar B b (dist g s) (dgp zbar B b g Φ s)) :
    tMap zbar B b g C Φ = Φ := by
  refine sce_of_rational h hs zbar B b g fun t i => ?_
  funext ω
  set v : ι → ℝ := fun k => forecast Φ s t k ω - 𝔼.E t (dgp zbar B b g Φ s (t + 1) k) ω
  have hv : B *ᵥ v = 0 := by
    funext i
    have h1 := congrFun (hree t i) ω
    simp only [dgp] at h1
    simp only [mulVec, dotProduct, v, Pi.zero_apply, mul_sub, Finset.sum_sub_distrib]
    have h2 : ∑ k, B i k * (forecast Φ s t k ω - zbar k) =
        ∑ k, B i k * (𝔼.E t (dgp zbar B b g Φ s (t + 1) k) ω - zbar k) := by linarith
    simp only [mul_sub, Finset.sum_sub_distrib] at h2
    linarith
  have := congrFun (eq_zero_of_mulVec_eq_zero hB hv) i
  simpa [v, sub_eq_zero] using this

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 271: a process affine in the state, `z_t = z̄ + p + Q s_t`. -/
def affProc (zbar p : ι → ℝ) (Q : Matrix ι S ℝ) (s : ℕ → S → Ω → ℝ) (t : ℕ) (i : ι) :
    Ω → ℝ :=
  affRV (zbar i + p i) (Q i) (s t)

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 271: an affine process is a rational-expectations equilibrium iff its
coefficients satisfy `B p = p` and `Q = B Q C + b g′` (non-degenerate state). -/
theorem affine_isREE_iff {𝔼 : ExpectationSystem Ω} {C : Matrix S S ℝ} {s e : ℕ → S → Ω → ℝ}
    (h : StateLaw 𝔼 C s e) (hs : Nondegenerate s) (zbar : ι → ℝ) (B : Matrix ι ι ℝ)
    (b : ι → ℝ) (g : S → ℝ) (p : ι → ℝ) (Q : Matrix ι S ℝ) :
    IsREE 𝔼 zbar B b (dist g s) (affProc zbar p Q s) ↔
      B *ᵥ p = p ∧ Q = B * Q * C + vecMulVec b g := by
  have hE : ∀ t k, 𝔼.E t (affProc zbar p Q s (t + 1) k) = forecast (zbar + p, Q * C) s t k := by
    intro t k
    rw [affProc, E_affRV_succ h]
    rfl
  have hrhs : ∀ t i, (fun ω => zbar i + ∑ k, B i k *
      (𝔼.E t (affProc zbar p Q s (t + 1) k) ω - zbar k) + b i * dist g s t ω) =
      affRV (zbar i + (B *ᵥ p) i) ((B * (Q * C) + vecMulVec b g) i) (s t) := by
    intro t i
    simp_rw [hE]
    have := dgp_eq zbar B b g (zbar + p, Q * C) s t i
    simp only [add_sub_cancel_left] at this
    exact this
  unfold IsREE
  simp_rw [hrhs]
  constructor
  · intro hr
    have key : ∀ i, zbar i + p i = zbar i + (B *ᵥ p) i ∧ Q i = (B * (Q * C) + vecMulVec b g) i :=
      fun i => affRV_inj hs fun t => hr t i
    refine ⟨funext fun i => ((add_right_inj _).mp (key i).1).symm, ?_⟩
    ext i j
    have := congrFun (key i).2 j
    rw [Matrix.mul_assoc]
    exact this
  · rintro ⟨hp, hQ⟩ t i
    unfold affProc
    rw [hp, Matrix.mul_assoc] at *
    rw [← hQ]

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 271: the coefficients of an affine r.e.e. give a fixed point of `T`:
`T(z̄ + p, Q C) = (z̄ + p, Q C)`. -/
theorem fixed_of_ree_coeffs (zbar : ι → ℝ) (B : Matrix ι ι ℝ) (b : ι → ℝ) (g : S → ℝ)
    (C : Matrix S S ℝ) {p : ι → ℝ} {Q : Matrix ι S ℝ} (hp : B *ᵥ p = p)
    (hQ : Q = B * Q * C + vecMulVec b g) :
    tMap zbar B b g C (zbar + p, Q * C) = (zbar + p, Q * C) := by
  simp only [tMap, add_sub_cancel_left, hp, Prod.mk.injEq, true_and]
  conv_rhs => rw [hQ]
  rw [Matrix.mul_assoc]

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 271: conversely a fixed point `Φ̄` of `T` gives the coefficients
`p = Φ̄₀ − z̄`, `Q = B Φ̄ₛ + b g′` of an affine r.e.e., and `Φ̄ = (z̄ + p, Q C)`. -/
theorem ree_coeffs_of_fixed (zbar : ι → ℝ) (B : Matrix ι ι ℝ) (b : ι → ℝ) (g : S → ℝ)
    (C : Matrix S S ℝ) {Φ : Belief ι S} (hfix : tMap zbar B b g C Φ = Φ) :
    B *ᵥ (Φ.1 - zbar) = Φ.1 - zbar ∧
      B * Φ.2 + vecMulVec b g = B * (B * Φ.2 + vecMulVec b g) * C + vecMulVec b g ∧
      (zbar + (Φ.1 - zbar), (B * Φ.2 + vecMulVec b g) * C) = Φ := by
  have h1 : zbar + B *ᵥ (Φ.1 - zbar) = Φ.1 := congrArg Prod.fst hfix
  have h2 : (B * Φ.2 + vecMulVec b g) * C = Φ.2 := congrArg Prod.snd hfix
  refine ⟨?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · exact (sub_eq_iff_eq_add'.mpr h1.symm).symm
  · rw [Matrix.mul_assoc, h2]
  · rw [add_sub_cancel, h2]

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 271: the d.g.p. generated by a fixed point is the affine process with the
coefficients of `ree_coeffs_of_fixed`. -/
theorem dgp_eq_affProc_of_fixed (zbar : ι → ℝ) (B : Matrix ι ι ℝ) (b : ι → ℝ) (g : S → ℝ)
    (C : Matrix S S ℝ) {Φ : Belief ι S} (hfix : tMap zbar B b g C Φ = Φ)
    (s : ℕ → S → Ω → ℝ) :
    dgp zbar B b g Φ s = affProc zbar (Φ.1 - zbar) (B * Φ.2 + vecMulVec b g) s := by
  funext t i
  rw [dgp_eq, affProc, (ree_coeffs_of_fixed zbar B b g C hfix).1]

/-! ### Existence and uniqueness of the fixed point -/

/-- Woodford (2003), (C.29) p. 684: the Sylvester equation `X = B X C + R` has exactly one
solution when `1` is not an eigenvalue of `C′ ⊗ B` (vectorised, `(I − C′ ⊗ B) vec X = vec R`). -/
theorem sylvester_existsUnique (B : Matrix ι ι ℝ)
    (C : Matrix S S ℝ) (R : Matrix ι S ℝ)
    (hK : ¬ KroneckerSpectrum.IsEig ((Cᵀ ⊗ₖ B).map Complex.ofReal) 1) :
    ∃! X : Matrix ι S ℝ, X = B * X * C + R := by
  classical
  have hdet := KroneckerSpectrum.det_one_sub_ne_zero _ hK
  set K := Cᵀ ⊗ₖ B with hKdef
  have key : ∀ X : Matrix ι S ℝ, (1 - K) *ᵥ vec X = vec (X - B * X * C) := fun X => by
    rw [sub_mulVec, one_mulVec, hKdef, KroneckerSpectrum.vec_mul_mul, vec_sub]
  have hiff : ∀ X : Matrix ι S ℝ, X = B * X * C + R ↔ (1 - K) *ᵥ vec X = vec R := fun X => by
    rw [key, vec_inj, sub_eq_iff_eq_add', add_comm]
  set X₀ : Matrix ι S ℝ := Matrix.of fun i j => ((1 - K)⁻¹ *ᵥ vec R) (j, i) with hX₀
  have hvec : vec X₀ = (1 - K)⁻¹ *ᵥ vec R := by
    funext ⟨j, i⟩
    rfl
  have hX₀R : (1 - K) *ᵥ vec X₀ = vec R := by
    rw [hvec, mulVec_mulVec, mul_nonsing_inv _ (isUnit_iff_ne_zero.mpr hdet), one_mulVec]
  refine ⟨X₀, (hiff X₀).mpr hX₀R, fun Y hY => ?_⟩
  have hY' : Y = B * Y * C + R := hY
  rw [hiff] at hY'
  apply vec_inj.mp
  have h0 : (1 - K) *ᵥ (vec Y - vec X₀) = 0 := by rw [mulVec_sub, hY', hX₀R, sub_self]
  exact sub_eq_zero.mp (eq_zero_of_mulVec_eq_zero hdet h0)

/-- Woodford (2003), (2.26)–(2.27): `Φ` is a fixed point of the regression `T`-map iff
`(I − B)(Φ₀ − z̄) = 0` and `Φₛ = B Φₛ C + b g′ C`. -/
theorem tMap_fixed_iff [DecidableEq ι] (zbar : ι → ℝ) (B : Matrix ι ι ℝ) (b : ι → ℝ)
    (g : S → ℝ) (C : Matrix S S ℝ) (Φ : Belief ι S) :
    tMap zbar B b g C Φ = Φ ↔
      (1 - B) *ᵥ (Φ.1 - zbar) = 0 ∧ Φ.2 = B * Φ.2 * C + vecMulVec b g * C := by
  rw [Prod.ext_iff, ← Tmap_fixed_iff_one_sub]
  refine and_congr Iff.rfl ?_
  simp only [tMap]
  rw [Matrix.add_mul]
  exact eq_comm

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 271: "the fixed point `Φ̄` of this mapping is generically unique": it
exists and is unique when `1` is not an eigenvalue of `B` nor of `C′ ⊗ B`; its intercept is
`z̄`. -/
theorem fixed_existsUnique [DecidableEq ι] (zbar : ι → ℝ) (B : Matrix ι ι ℝ)
    (b : ι → ℝ) (g : S → ℝ) (C : Matrix S S ℝ) (hB : (1 - B).det ≠ 0)
    (hK : ¬ KroneckerSpectrum.IsEig ((Cᵀ ⊗ₖ B).map Complex.ofReal) 1) :
    ∃! Φ : Belief ι S, tMap zbar B b g C Φ = Φ := by
  obtain ⟨X, hX, hXu⟩ := sylvester_existsUnique B C (vecMulVec b g * C) hK
  refine ⟨(zbar, X), ?_, ?_⟩
  · change tMap zbar B b g C (zbar, X) = (zbar, X)
    rw [tMap_fixed_iff]
    exact ⟨by simp, hX⟩
  · intro Φ hΦ
    change tMap zbar B b g C Φ = Φ at hΦ
    rw [tMap_fixed_iff] at hΦ
    have h1 : Φ.1 = zbar := sub_eq_zero.mp (eq_zero_of_mulVec_eq_zero hB hΦ.1)
    have h2 : Φ.2 = X := hXu Φ.2 hΦ.2
    exact Prod.ext h1 h2

/-- Woodford (2003), pp. 684–685: if every eigenvalue of `C` has modulus `< 1` and every
eigenvalue of `B` modulus `≤ 1`, then `1` is not an eigenvalue of `C′ ⊗ B`. -/
theorem not_isEig_one_kronecker {B : Matrix ι ι ℝ}
    {C : Matrix S S ℝ}
    (hC : ∀ ρ, KroneckerSpectrum.IsEig (C.map Complex.ofReal) ρ → ‖ρ‖ < 1)
    (hB : ∀ l, KroneckerSpectrum.IsEig (B.map Complex.ofReal) l → ‖l‖ ≤ 1) :
    ¬ KroneckerSpectrum.IsEig ((Cᵀ ⊗ₖ B).map Complex.ofReal) 1 := by
  classical
  intro h
  rw [KroneckerSpectrum.kronecker_map_ofReal, KroneckerSpectrum.transpose_map_ofReal] at h
  obtain ⟨ρ, l, hρ, hl, h1⟩ := KroneckerSpectrum.exists_of_isEig_kronecker h
  rw [KroneckerSpectrum.isEig_transpose_iff] at hρ
  have h2 := congrArg norm h1
  rw [norm_one, norm_mul] at h2
  nlinarith [hC ρ hρ, hB l hl, norm_nonneg ρ, norm_nonneg l]

/-! ### The fixed point is the unique bounded r.e.e. -/

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 268: an r.e.e. in deviations from `z̄` solves the forward system
`y_t = B E_t y_{t+1} + b u_t` of the core `Solves`. -/
theorem solves_of_isREE {𝔼 : ExpectationSystem Ω} {zbar : Fin 2 → ℝ}
    {B : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℝ} {b : Fin 2 → ℝ} {u : ℕ → Ω → ℝ} {z : ℕ → Fin 2 → Ω → ℝ}
    (hz : IsREE 𝔼 zbar B b u z) :
    𝔼.Solves B (fun t i => b i • u t) (fun t i => z t i - fun _ => zbar i) := by
  intro t i
  change z t i - _ = _
  rw [hz t i]
  funext ω
  simp only [map_sub, 𝔼.const, Fin.sum_univ_two, Pi.sub_apply, Pi.add_apply, Pi.smul_apply,
    smul_eq_mul]
  ring

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 268: under the Schur–Cohn condition on `B` there is at most one bounded
adapted r.e.e. -/
theorem ree_unique_bounded {𝔼 : ExpectationSystem Ω} {zbar : Fin 2 → ℝ}
    {B : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℝ} (hS : SchurStable (tr2 B) (det2 B)) {b : Fin 2 → ℝ}
    {u : ℕ → Ω → ℝ} {z₁ z₂ : ℕ → Fin 2 → Ω → ℝ}
    (h₁ : IsREE 𝔼 zbar B b u z₁) (h₂ : IsREE 𝔼 zbar B b u z₂)
    (ha₁ : ∀ t i, 𝔼.E t (z₁ t i) = z₁ t i) (ha₂ : ∀ t i, 𝔼.E t (z₂ t i) = z₂ t i)
    (hb₁ : ∃ M, ∀ t i ω, |z₁ t i ω| ≤ M) (hb₂ : ∃ M, ∀ t i ω, |z₂ t i ω| ≤ M) : z₁ = z₂ := by
  have hbd : ∀ z : ℕ → Fin 2 → Ω → ℝ, (∃ M, ∀ t i ω, |z t i ω| ≤ M) →
      BoundedVec (fun t i => z t i - fun _ => zbar i) := by
    rintro z ⟨M, hM⟩
    refine ⟨M + (|zbar 0| + |zbar 1|), fun t i ω => ?_⟩
    have hz := hM t i ω
    have h0 : |zbar i| ≤ |zbar 0| + |zbar 1| := by fin_cases i <;> simp
    change |z t i ω - zbar i| ≤ _
    linarith [abs_sub (z t i ω) (zbar i)]
  have had : ∀ z : ℕ → Fin 2 → Ω → ℝ, (∀ t i, 𝔼.E t (z t i) = z t i) →
      𝔼.AdaptedVec (fun t i => z t i - fun _ => zbar i) := by
    intro z hz t i
    simp only [map_sub, hz t i, 𝔼.const]
  have := 𝔼.system_unique hS (solves_of_isREE h₁) (solves_of_isREE h₂) (had z₁ ha₁)
    (had z₂ ha₂) (hbd z₁ hb₁) (hbd z₂ hb₂)
  funext t i
  have h := congrFun (congrFun this t) i
  simpa using h

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 270: the d.g.p. generated by any belief is adapted. -/
theorem dgp_adapted {𝔼 : ExpectationSystem Ω} {C : Matrix S S ℝ} {s e : ℕ → S → Ω → ℝ}
    (h : StateLaw 𝔼 C s e) (zbar : ι → ℝ) (B : Matrix ι ι ℝ) (b : ι → ℝ) (g : S → ℝ)
    (Φ : Belief ι S) (t : ℕ) (i : ι) :
    𝔼.E t (dgp zbar B b g Φ s t i) = dgp zbar B b g Φ s t i := by
  rw [dgp_eq]
  exact E_affRV_of_known 𝔼 _ _ (h.1 t)

omit [Fintype ι] in
/-- Woodford (2003), p. 270: an affine function of a bounded state is bounded, uniformly over
components. -/
theorem affRV_bounded [Finite ι] {s : ℕ → S → Ω → ℝ} (hs : ∃ M, ∀ t j ω, |s t j ω| ≤ M)
    (c : ι → ℝ) (a : ι → S → ℝ) : ∃ M, ∀ t i ω, |affRV (c i) (a i) (s t) ω| ≤ M := by
  have : Fintype ι := Fintype.ofFinite ι
  obtain ⟨M, hM⟩ := hs
  set M₀ := max M 0
  refine ⟨∑ i, (|c i| + ∑ j, |a i j| * M₀), fun t i ω => ?_⟩
  have hle : |affRV (c i) (a i) (s t) ω| ≤ |c i| + ∑ j, |a i j| * M₀ := by
    unfold affRV
    refine (abs_add_le _ _).trans (add_le_add_right ?_ _)
    refine (Finset.abs_sum_le_sum_abs _ _).trans (Finset.sum_le_sum fun j _ => ?_)
    rw [abs_mul]
    exact mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left ((hM t j ω).trans (le_max_left _ _)) (abs_nonneg _)
  refine hle.trans (Finset.single_le_sum (f := fun i => |c i| + ∑ j, |a i j| * M₀)
    (fun i _ => ?_) (Finset.mem_univ i))
  have : 0 ≤ M₀ := le_max_right _ _
  positivity

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 271: "in the case that (2.7) is satisfied, so that the r.e.e. is
determinate, the fixed point of `T` is just the unique bounded r.e.e.": with `B` Schur-stable
and a bounded state, the d.g.p. of a fixed point is a bounded adapted r.e.e., and every bounded
adapted r.e.e. coincides with it. -/
theorem fixed_unique_bounded_ree {𝔼 : ExpectationSystem Ω} {C : Matrix S S ℝ}
    {s e : ℕ → S → Ω → ℝ} (h : StateLaw 𝔼 C s e) (hsb : ∃ M, ∀ t j ω, |s t j ω| ≤ M)
    (zbar : Fin 2 → ℝ) {B : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℝ} (hS : SchurStable (tr2 B) (det2 B))
    (b : Fin 2 → ℝ) (g : S → ℝ) {Φ : Belief (Fin 2) S} (hfix : tMap zbar B b g C Φ = Φ) :
    IsREE 𝔼 zbar B b (dist g s) (dgp zbar B b g Φ s) ∧
      (∀ t i, 𝔼.E t (dgp zbar B b g Φ s t i) = dgp zbar B b g Φ s t i) ∧
      (∃ M, ∀ t i ω, |dgp zbar B b g Φ s t i ω| ≤ M) ∧
      ∀ z : ℕ → Fin 2 → Ω → ℝ, IsREE 𝔼 zbar B b (dist g s) z →
        (∀ t i, 𝔼.E t (z t i) = z t i) → (∃ M, ∀ t i ω, |z t i ω| ≤ M) →
          z = dgp zbar B b g Φ s := by
  have hree := sce_isREE h zbar B b g hfix
  have had := dgp_adapted h zbar B b g Φ
  have hbd : ∃ M, ∀ t i ω, |dgp zbar B b g Φ s t i ω| ≤ M := by
    obtain ⟨M, hM⟩ := affRV_bounded hsb (fun i => zbar i + (B *ᵥ (Φ.1 - zbar)) i)
      (fun i => (B * Φ.2 + vecMulVec b g) i)
    exact ⟨M, fun t i ω => by rw [dgp_eq]; exact hM t i ω⟩
  exact ⟨hree, had, hbd, fun z hz hza hzb => ree_unique_bounded hS hz hree hza had hzb hbd⟩

/-! ### Vectorisation and the Jacobian `DT = blockdiag(B, C′ ⊗ B)` -/

/-- Woodford (2003), App. C.7, p. 684: the vectorised belief `(Φ₀, vec Φₛ)`. -/
def vecBelief (Φ : Belief ι S) : ι ⊕ (S × ι) → ℝ := Sum.elim Φ.1 (vec Φ.2)

/-- Woodford (2003), App. C.7, p. 684: the inverse of `vecBelief`. -/
def unvecBelief (v : ι ⊕ (S × ι) → ℝ) : Belief ι S :=
  (fun i => v (Sum.inl i), Matrix.of fun i j => v (Sum.inr (j, i)))

omit [Fintype ι] [Fintype S] in
/-- Woodford (2003), App. C.7, p. 684: `vecBelief` and `unvecBelief` are inverse. -/
theorem vecBelief_unvecBelief (v : ι ⊕ (S × ι) → ℝ) : vecBelief (unvecBelief v) = v := by
  funext x
  rcases x with i | ⟨j, i⟩ <;> rfl

omit [Fintype ι] [Fintype S] in
/-- Woodford (2003), App. C.7, p. 684: `unvecBelief` and `vecBelief` are inverse. -/
theorem unvecBelief_vecBelief (Φ : Belief ι S) : unvecBelief (vecBelief Φ) = Φ := rfl

/-- Woodford (2003), App. C.7, p. 684: the Jacobian `DT = blockdiag(B, C′ ⊗ B)`. -/
def dT (B : Matrix ι ι ℝ) (C : Matrix S S ℝ) : Matrix (ι ⊕ (S × ι)) (ι ⊕ (S × ι)) ℝ :=
  fromBlocks B 0 0 (Cᵀ ⊗ₖ B)

/-- Woodford (2003), App. C.7, p. 684: the regression `T`-map in vectorised coordinates. -/
def tVec (zbar : ι → ℝ) (B : Matrix ι ι ℝ) (b : ι → ℝ) (g : S → ℝ) (C : Matrix S S ℝ)
    (v : ι ⊕ (S × ι) → ℝ) : ι ⊕ (S × ι) → ℝ :=
  vecBelief (tMap zbar B b g C (unvecBelief v))

/-- Woodford (2003), App. C.7, p. 684: the constant term of the vectorised `T`-map. -/
def tVecConst (zbar : ι → ℝ) (B : Matrix ι ι ℝ) (b : ι → ℝ) (g : S → ℝ) (C : Matrix S S ℝ) :
    ι ⊕ (S × ι) → ℝ :=
  vecBelief (zbar - B *ᵥ zbar, vecMulVec b g * C)

/-- Woodford (2003), (C.28)–(C.29) p. 684: the vectorised `T`-map is affine,
`vec T(Φ̂) = const + blockdiag(B, C′ ⊗ B) vec Φ̂`. -/
theorem tVec_eq (zbar : ι → ℝ) (B : Matrix ι ι ℝ) (b : ι → ℝ) (g : S → ℝ) (C : Matrix S S ℝ)
    (v : ι ⊕ (S × ι) → ℝ) :
    tVec zbar B b g C v = tVecConst zbar B b g C + dT B C *ᵥ v := by
  set Φ := unvecBelief v with hΦ
  have hv : v = vecBelief Φ := (vecBelief_unvecBelief v).symm
  have hr : v ∘ Sum.inr = vec Φ.2 := by funext ⟨j, i⟩; rfl
  have hl : v ∘ Sum.inl = Φ.1 := rfl
  rw [dT, fromBlocks_mulVec, hr, hl, KroneckerSpectrum.vec_mul_mul]
  funext x
  rcases x with i | ⟨j, i⟩
  · simp only [tVec, tVecConst, tMap, vecBelief, Sum.elim_inl, Pi.add_apply, Pi.sub_apply,
      zero_mulVec, add_zero, mulVec_sub, ← hΦ]
    ring
  · simp only [tVec, tVecConst, tMap, vecBelief, Sum.elim_inr, Pi.add_apply, zero_mulVec,
      zero_add, ← hΦ]
    rw [Matrix.add_mul, vec_add, Pi.add_apply, add_comm]

/-- Woodford (2003), App. C.7, p. 684: the vectorised `T`-map has Fréchet derivative
`DT = blockdiag(B, C′ ⊗ B)` at every point. -/
theorem hasFDerivAt_tVec [DecidableEq ι] [DecidableEq S] (zbar : ι → ℝ) (B : Matrix ι ι ℝ)
    (b : ι → ℝ) (g : S → ℝ) (C : Matrix S S ℝ) (v : ι ⊕ (S × ι) → ℝ) :
    HasFDerivAt (tVec zbar B b g C)
      (LinearMap.toContinuousLinearMap (Matrix.toLin' (dT B C))) v := by
  have h : tVec zbar B b g C = fun w => tVecConst zbar B b g C + dT B C *ᵥ w :=
    funext (tVec_eq zbar B b g C)
  rw [h]
  exact hasFDerivAt_affine _ _ v

/-- Woodford (2003), App. C.7, p. 684: a fixed point `Φ̄` of `T` is E-stable (in the sense of
`EStableAt`, through the Fréchet derivative of the vectorised map) iff `DT` is E-stable. -/
theorem eStableAt_tVec_iff [DecidableEq ι] [DecidableEq S] (zbar : ι → ℝ) (B : Matrix ι ι ℝ)
    (b : ι → ℝ) (g : S → ℝ) (C : Matrix S S ℝ) {Φ : Belief ι S}
    (hfix : tMap zbar B b g C Φ = Φ) :
    EStableAt (tVec zbar B b g C) (vecBelief Φ) ↔ EStable (dT B C) := by
  have h : tVec zbar B b g C = fun w => tVecConst zbar B b g C + dT B C *ᵥ w :=
    funext (tVec_eq zbar B b g C)
  have hfix' : tVecConst zbar B b g C + dT B C *ᵥ vecBelief Φ = vecBelief Φ := by
    rw [← tVec_eq, tVec, unvecBelief_vecBelief, hfix]
  rw [h]
  exact eStableAt_affine_iff _ _ _ hfix'

omit [Fintype ι] [Fintype S] in
/-- Woodford (2003), App. C.7, p. 684: complexifying `DT` gives
`blockdiag(B_ℂ, C_ℂ′ ⊗ B_ℂ)`. -/
theorem dT_map_ofReal (B : Matrix ι ι ℝ) (C : Matrix S S ℝ) :
    (dT B C).map Complex.ofReal =
      fromBlocks (B.map Complex.ofReal) 0 0
        ((C.map Complex.ofReal)ᵀ ⊗ₖ B.map Complex.ofReal) := by
  rw [dT, KroneckerSpectrum.fromBlocks_map_ofReal, KroneckerSpectrum.kronecker_map_ofReal,
    KroneckerSpectrum.transpose_map_ofReal]

/-- Woodford (2003), App. C.7, pp. 684–685 (sufficiency): if every eigenvalue of `B` and of `C`
has modulus less than one, `DT` is E-stable (every eigenvalue of `DT` has modulus, hence real
part, less than one). -/
theorem eStable_dT_of [DecidableEq ι] [DecidableEq S] {B : Matrix ι ι ℝ} {C : Matrix S S ℝ}
    (hB : ∀ l, KroneckerSpectrum.IsEig (B.map Complex.ofReal) l → ‖l‖ < 1)
    (hC : ∀ ρ, KroneckerSpectrum.IsEig (C.map Complex.ofReal) ρ → ‖ρ‖ < 1) :
    EStable (dT B C) := by
  rw [eStable_iff]
  intro μ hμ
  rw [dT_map_ofReal, KroneckerSpectrum.isEig_fromBlocks_iff] at hμ
  refine lt_of_le_of_lt (Complex.re_le_norm μ) ?_
  rcases hμ with hμ | hμ
  · exact hB μ hμ
  · refine KroneckerSpectrum.norm_lt_one_of_isEig_kronecker (fun ρ hρ => ?_) hB hμ
    exact hC ρ ((KroneckerSpectrum.isEig_transpose_iff _ _).mp hρ)

/-- Woodford (2003), App. C.7, p. 684 (necessity): the eigenvalues of `B` are eigenvalues of
`DT`, so E-stability of `DT` implies E-stability of `B`. -/
theorem eStable_of_eStable_dT [DecidableEq ι] [DecidableEq S] {B : Matrix ι ι ℝ}
    {C : Matrix S S ℝ} (h : EStable (dT B C)) : EStable B := by
  rw [eStable_iff] at h ⊢
  intro μ hμ
  apply h μ
  rw [dT_map_ofReal, KroneckerSpectrum.isEig_fromBlocks_iff]
  exact Or.inl hμ

end Regression

/-! ### Proposition 4.9 -/

namespace BullardMitra

open Regression

variable {β κ σ φπ φx : ℝ} {S : Type*} [Fintype S]

/-- Woodford (2003), App. C.7, p. 684 (error E28): **(C.18) is necessary for E-stability** of
the regression r.e.e. The book prints "necessary for determinacy"; that sentence is true
(Prop. 4.3, `determinate_taylorB_iff`) but is not what the argument establishes, which is
necessity for E-stability. No assumption on `C` is needed. -/
theorem taylor_of_eStable_dT [DecidableEq S] (hβ0 : 0 < β) (hβ1 : β < 1) (hκ : 0 < κ) (hσ : 0 < σ)
    (hπ : 0 ≤ φπ) (hx : 0 ≤ φx) (C : Matrix S S ℝ)
    (h : EStable (dT (taylorB β σ κ φπ φx) C)) : 1 < taylorLHS β κ φπ φx :=
  (prop_4_8 hβ0 hβ1 hσ hκ hπ hx).mp (eStable_of_eStable_dT h)

/-- Woodford (2003), **Proposition 4.9** (p. 271; proof App. C.7, pp. 683–685): with the
Bullard–Mitra temporary equilibrium, a Taylor rule with `φ_π, φ_x ≥ 0`, and regression
learning on a stationary state (every eigenvalue of `C` inside the unit circle), the Jacobian
`DT = blockdiag(B, C′ ⊗ B)` is E-stable iff the Taylor principle (2.7) holds. -/
theorem prop_4_9 [DecidableEq S] (hβ0 : 0 < β) (hβ1 : β < 1) (hκ : 0 < κ) (hσ : 0 < σ) (hπ : 0 ≤ φπ)
    (hx : 0 ≤ φx) (C : Matrix S S ℝ)
    (hC : ∀ ρ, KroneckerSpectrum.IsEig (C.map Complex.ofReal) ρ → ‖ρ‖ < 1) :
    EStable (dT (taylorB β σ κ φπ φx) C) ↔ 1 < taylorLHS β κ φπ φx := by
  refine ⟨taylor_of_eStable_dT hβ0 hβ1 hκ hσ hπ hx C, fun hT => ?_⟩
  exact eStable_dT_of (fun l hl => norm_lt_one_of_isEig_taylorB hβ0 hβ1 hκ hσ hπ hx hT hl) hC

/-- Woodford (2003), **Proposition 4.9** at the r.e.e. itself: any fixed point `Φ̄` of the
regression `T`-map is E-stable (Fréchet derivative of the vectorised map) iff (2.7) holds. -/
theorem prop_4_9_at [DecidableEq S] (hβ0 : 0 < β) (hβ1 : β < 1) (hκ : 0 < κ) (hσ : 0 < σ)
    (hπ : 0 ≤ φπ) (hx : 0 ≤ φx) (zbar : Fin 2 → ℝ) (g : S → ℝ) (C : Matrix S S ℝ)
    (hC : ∀ ρ, KroneckerSpectrum.IsEig (C.map Complex.ofReal) ρ → ‖ρ‖ < 1)
    {Φ : Belief (Fin 2) S} (hfix : tMap zbar (taylorB β σ κ φπ φx) (taylorb σ κ φπ φx) g C Φ = Φ) :
    EStableAt (tVec zbar (taylorB β σ κ φπ φx) (taylorb σ κ φπ φx) g C) (vecBelief Φ) ↔
      1 < taylorLHS β κ φπ φx := by
  rw [eStableAt_tVec_iff _ _ _ _ _ hfix, prop_4_9 hβ0 hβ1 hκ hσ hπ hx C hC]

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 271: under (2.7) and a stationary state the r.e.e. `Φ̄` (fixed point of
the regression `T`-map) exists and is unique. -/
theorem fixed_existsUnique_of_taylor (hβ0 : 0 < β) (hβ1 : β < 1) (hκ : 0 < κ) (hσ : 0 < σ)
    (hπ : 0 ≤ φπ) (hx : 0 ≤ φx) (hT : 1 < taylorLHS β κ φπ φx) (zbar : Fin 2 → ℝ)
    (g : S → ℝ) (C : Matrix S S ℝ)
    (hC : ∀ ρ, KroneckerSpectrum.IsEig (C.map Complex.ofReal) ρ → ‖ρ‖ < 1) :
    ∃! Φ : Belief (Fin 2) S, tMap zbar (taylorB β σ κ φπ φx) (taylorb σ κ φπ φx) g C Φ = Φ := by
  have hD := taylorDelta_pos hσ hκ hπ hx
  have hB : (1 - taylorB β σ κ φπ φx).det ≠ 0 := by
    rw [det_one_sub_taylorB]
    have hkey : 1 - tr2 (taylorB β σ κ φπ φx) + det2 (taylorB β σ κ φπ φx) =
        κ * σ * (taylorLHS β κ φπ φx - 1) / taylorDelta σ κ φπ φx := by
      linear_combination taylorB_one_sub (β := β) (φπ := φπ) (φx := φx) hκ.ne' hD.ne'
    rw [hkey]
    have : 0 < taylorLHS β κ φπ φx - 1 := by linarith
    positivity
  exact fixed_existsUnique zbar _ _ g C hB (not_isEig_one_kronecker hC
    fun l hl => (norm_lt_one_of_isEig_taylorB hβ0 hβ1 hκ hσ hπ hx hT hl).le)

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 271: under (2.7) the fixed point of `T` generates the unique bounded
r.e.e. (bounded state). -/
theorem fixed_unique_bounded_ree_of_taylor {Ω : Type*} {𝔼 : ExpectationSystem Ω}
    {C : Matrix S S ℝ} {s e : ℕ → S → Ω → ℝ} (h : StateLaw 𝔼 C s e)
    (hsb : ∃ M, ∀ t j ω, |s t j ω| ≤ M) (hβ0 : 0 < β) (hβ1 : β < 1) (hκ : 0 < κ)
    (hσ : 0 < σ) (hπ : 0 ≤ φπ) (hx : 0 ≤ φx) (hT : 1 < taylorLHS β κ φπ φx)
    (zbar : Fin 2 → ℝ) (g : S → ℝ) {Φ : Belief (Fin 2) S}
    (hfix : tMap zbar (taylorB β σ κ φπ φx) (taylorb σ κ φπ φx) g C Φ = Φ) (z : ℕ → Fin 2 → Ω → ℝ)
    (hz : IsREE 𝔼 zbar (taylorB β σ κ φπ φx) (taylorb σ κ φπ φx) (dist g s) z)
    (hza : ∀ t i, 𝔼.E t (z t i) = z t i) (hzb : ∃ M, ∀ t i ω, |z t i ω| ≤ M) :
    z = dgp zbar (taylorB β σ κ φπ φx) (taylorb σ κ φπ φx) g Φ s :=
  (fixed_unique_bounded_ree h hsb zbar ((taylorB_schurStable_iff hβ0 hβ1 hσ hκ hπ hx).mpr hT)
    _ g hfix).2.2.2 z hz hza hzb

/-! ### Phase diagrams: footnotes 38–39 and p. 268 -/

/-- Woodford (2003), Figures 4.3–4.4 and p. 268: `π̇ᵉ` of the learning ODE for the intercept
beliefs, in deviations `(πᵉ − π̄, xᵉ − x̄)`. -/
noncomputable def piDot (β κ σ φπ φx pe xe : ℝ) : ℝ :=
  (taylorB β σ κ φπ φx 0 0 - 1) * pe + taylorB β σ κ φπ φx 0 1 * xe

/-- Woodford (2003), Figures 4.3–4.4 and p. 268: `ẋᵉ` of the learning ODE for the intercept
beliefs, in deviations. -/
noncomputable def xDot (β κ σ φπ φx pe xe : ℝ) : ℝ :=
  taylorB β σ κ φπ φx 1 0 * pe + (taylorB β σ κ φπ φx 1 1 - 1) * xe

/-- Woodford (2003), (2.20) and (C.28): the intercept part of `T(Φ) − Φ` is `(π̇ᵉ, ẋᵉ)`. -/
theorem intercept_ode (zbar : Fin 2 → ℝ) (b : Fin 2 → ℝ) (g : S → ℝ) (C : Matrix S S ℝ)
    (Φ : Belief (Fin 2) S) :
    (tMap zbar (taylorB β σ κ φπ φx) b g C Φ).1 - Φ.1 =
      ![piDot β κ σ φπ φx (Φ.1 0 - zbar 0) (Φ.1 1 - zbar 1),
        xDot β κ σ φπ φx (Φ.1 0 - zbar 0) (Φ.1 1 - zbar 1)] := by
  funext i
  fin_cases i <;>
    simp [tMap, mulVec, dotProduct, Fin.sum_univ_two, piDot, xDot] <;> ring

/-- Woodford (2003), footnote 38 (common numerator): `B₀₀ − 1 = N/Δ` with
`N = κσ(1 − φ_π) − (1 − β)(1 + σφ_x/4)`. -/
theorem taylorB00_sub_one (hd : taylorDelta σ κ φπ φx ≠ 0) :
    taylorB β σ κ φπ φx 0 0 - 1 =
      (κ * σ * (1 - φπ) - (1 - β) * (1 + σ * φx / 4)) / taylorDelta σ κ φπ φx := by
  simp only [taylorB, of_apply, cons_val', cons_val_zero, empty_val', cons_val_fin_one]
  field_simp
  unfold taylorDelta
  ring

/-- Woodford (2003), footnote 38: the threshold `1 − (1 − β)/(κσ)` minus the left side of
(2.7) is `N/(κσ)`, with the same numerator `N` as `B₀₀ − 1`. -/
theorem thr_sub_taylorLHS (hκ : κ ≠ 0) (hσ : σ ≠ 0) :
    1 - (1 - β) / (κ * σ) - taylorLHS β κ φπ φx =
      (κ * σ * (1 - φπ) - (1 - β) * (1 + σ * φx / 4)) / (κ * σ) := by
  unfold taylorLHS
  field_simp
  ring

/-- Woodford (2003), **footnote 38**: `B₀₀ > 1` (so `π̇ᵉ > 0` at every point of the positive
`πᵉ`-axis) iff the left side of (2.7) is below `1 − (1 − β)/(κσ)`. -/
theorem taylorB00_gt_one_iff (hκ : 0 < κ) (hσ : 0 < σ) (hπ : 0 ≤ φπ) (hx : 0 ≤ φx) :
    1 < taylorB β σ κ φπ φx 0 0 ↔ taylorLHS β κ φπ φx < 1 - (1 - β) / (κ * σ) := by
  have hD := taylorDelta_pos hσ hκ hπ hx
  have h1 := taylorB00_sub_one (β := β) hD.ne'
  have h2 := thr_sub_taylorLHS (β := β) (φπ := φπ) (φx := φx) hκ.ne' hσ.ne'
  rw [← sub_pos, h1, div_pos_iff_of_pos_right hD, ← div_pos_iff_of_pos_right
    (mul_pos hκ hσ), ← h2, sub_pos]

/-- Woodford (2003), **footnote 38**: below the threshold, inflation expectations increase
everywhere in the positive orthant (`π̇ᵉ > 0` at every nonzero point with `πᵉ, xᵉ ≥ 0`). -/
theorem piDot_pos (hκ : 0 < κ) (hσ : 0 < σ) (hπ : 0 ≤ φπ) (hx : 0 ≤ φx)
    (hT : taylorLHS β κ φπ φx < 1 - (1 - β) / (κ * σ)) {pe xe : ℝ} (hpe : 0 ≤ pe)
    (hxe : 0 ≤ xe) (hne : 0 < pe ∨ 0 < xe) : 0 < piDot β κ σ φπ φx pe xe := by
  have hB := (taylorB00_gt_one_iff hκ hσ hπ hx).mpr hT
  have hD := taylorDelta_pos hσ hκ hπ hx
  have h01 : 0 < taylorB β σ κ φπ φx 0 1 := by
    simp only [taylorB, of_apply, cons_val', cons_val_one, cons_val_zero, empty_val',
      cons_val_fin_one]
    exact div_pos hκ hD
  unfold piDot
  rcases hne with h | h
  · have := mul_pos (sub_pos.mpr hB) h
    nlinarith [mul_nonneg h01.le hxe]
  · have := mul_pos h01 h
    nlinarith [mul_nonneg (sub_pos.mpr hB).le hpe]

/-- Woodford (2003), **footnote 38**: above the threshold the `π̇ᵉ = 0` locus passes through
the positive orthant (there are points with `πᵉ, xᵉ > 0` and `π̇ᵉ < 0`), as in Figure 4.3. -/
theorem exists_piDot_neg (hκ : 0 < κ) (hσ : 0 < σ) (hπ : 0 ≤ φπ) (hx : 0 ≤ φx)
    (hT : 1 - (1 - β) / (κ * σ) < taylorLHS β κ φπ φx) :
    ∃ pe xe, 0 < pe ∧ 0 < xe ∧ piDot β κ σ φπ φx pe xe < 0 := by
  have hB : taylorB β σ κ φπ φx 0 0 < 1 := by
    by_contra h
    rcases (not_lt.mp h).lt_or_eq with h | h
    · exact absurd ((taylorB00_gt_one_iff hκ hσ hπ hx).mp h) (not_lt.mpr hT.le)
    · have hD := taylorDelta_pos hσ hκ hπ hx
      have h1 := taylorB00_sub_one (β := β) hD.ne'
      rw [← h, sub_self, eq_comm, div_eq_zero_iff] at h1
      rcases h1 with h1 | h1
      · have h2 := thr_sub_taylorLHS (β := β) (φπ := φπ) (φx := φx) hκ.ne' hσ.ne'
        rw [h1, zero_div] at h2
        linarith
      · exact absurd h1 hD.ne'
  have hD := taylorDelta_pos hσ hκ hπ hx
  have h01 : 0 < taylorB β σ κ φπ φx 0 1 := by
    simp only [taylorB, of_apply, cons_val', cons_val_one, cons_val_zero, empty_val',
      cons_val_fin_one]
    exact div_pos hκ hD
  refine ⟨1, (1 - taylorB β σ κ φπ φx 0 0) / (2 * taylorB β σ κ φπ φx 0 1), one_pos,
    div_pos (by linarith) (by positivity), ?_⟩
  unfold piDot
  field_simp
  linarith

/-- Woodford (2003), **footnote 39**: `B₁₀ < 0` (so `ẋᵉ < 0` on the positive `πᵉ`-axis) iff
`φ_π > β⁻¹`. -/
theorem taylorB10_neg_iff (hβ0 : 0 < β) (hκ : 0 < κ) (hσ : 0 < σ) (hπ : 0 ≤ φπ) (hx : 0 ≤ φx) :
    taylorB β σ κ φπ φx 1 0 < 0 ↔ β⁻¹ < φπ := by
  have hD := taylorDelta_pos hσ hκ hπ hx
  simp only [taylorB, of_apply, cons_val', cons_val_one, cons_val_zero, empty_val',
    cons_val_fin_one]
  rw [div_neg_iff, inv_lt_iff_one_lt_mul₀' hβ0]
  constructor
  · rintro (⟨-, h⟩ | ⟨h1, -⟩)
    · exact absurd h (not_lt.mpr hD.le)
    · nlinarith
  · intro h
    exact Or.inr ⟨by nlinarith, hD⟩

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 268: `B₁₁ − 1 = −σ(φ_x/4 + κφ_π)/Δ`. -/
theorem taylorB11_sub_one (hd : taylorDelta σ κ φπ φx ≠ 0) :
    taylorB β σ κ φπ φx 1 1 - 1 = -(σ * (φx / 4 + κ * φπ)) / taylorDelta σ κ φπ φx := by
  simp only [taylorB, of_apply, cons_val', cons_val_one, empty_val', cons_val_fin_one]
  field_simp
  unfold taylorDelta
  ring

/-- Woodford (2003), **footnote 39**: when `φ_π > β⁻¹`, output-gap expectations decrease
everywhere in the positive orthant. -/
theorem xDot_neg (hβ0 : 0 < β) (hκ : 0 < κ) (hσ : 0 < σ) (hx : 0 ≤ φx)
    (hφ : β⁻¹ < φπ) {pe xe : ℝ} (hpe : 0 ≤ pe) (hxe : 0 ≤ xe) (hne : 0 < pe ∨ 0 < xe) :
    xDot β κ σ φπ φx pe xe < 0 := by
  have hπ : 0 < φπ := lt_trans (inv_pos.mpr hβ0) hφ
  have hD := taylorDelta_pos hσ hκ hπ.le hx
  have h10 := (taylorB10_neg_iff hβ0 hκ hσ hπ.le hx).mpr hφ
  have h11 : taylorB β σ κ φπ φx 1 1 - 1 < 0 := by
    rw [taylorB11_sub_one hD.ne']
    apply div_neg_of_neg_of_pos _ hD
    have : 0 < σ * (φx / 4 + κ * φπ) := by positivity
    linarith
  unfold xDot
  rcases hne with h | h
  · nlinarith [mul_nonpos_of_nonpos_of_nonneg h11.le hxe]
  · nlinarith [mul_nonpos_of_nonpos_of_nonneg h10.le hpe]

/-- Woodford (2003), **footnote 39**: when `φ_π < β⁻¹` the `ẋᵉ = 0` locus passes through the
positive orthant (there are points with `πᵉ, xᵉ > 0` and `ẋᵉ > 0`), as in Figure 4.4. -/
theorem exists_xDot_pos (hβ0 : 0 < β) (hκ : 0 < κ) (hσ : 0 < σ) (hπ : 0 ≤ φπ) (hx : 0 ≤ φx)
    (hφ : φπ < β⁻¹) : ∃ pe xe, 0 < pe ∧ 0 < xe ∧ 0 < xDot β κ σ φπ φx pe xe := by
  have hD := taylorDelta_pos hσ hκ hπ hx
  have h10 : 0 < taylorB β σ κ φπ φx 1 0 := by
    by_contra h
    rcases (not_lt.mp h).lt_or_eq with h | h
    · exact absurd ((taylorB10_neg_iff hβ0 hκ hσ hπ hx).mp h) (not_lt.mpr hφ.le)
    · simp only [taylorB, of_apply, cons_val', cons_val_one, cons_val_zero, empty_val',
        cons_val_fin_one, div_eq_zero_iff, mul_eq_zero] at h
      rcases h with (h | h) | h
      · exact absurd h hσ.ne'
      · have h3 := mul_lt_mul_of_pos_left hφ hβ0
        rw [mul_inv_cancel₀ hβ0.ne'] at h3
        linarith
      · exact absurd h hD.ne'
  set c := 1 - taylorB β σ κ φπ φx 1 1 with hc
  have hc0 : 0 ≤ c := by
    rw [hc, ← neg_sub, taylorB11_sub_one hD.ne', neg_div, neg_neg]
    positivity
  refine ⟨1, taylorB β σ κ φπ φx 1 0 / (2 * (c + 1)), one_pos, by positivity, ?_⟩
  unfold xDot
  have hxe : (taylorB β σ κ φπ φx 1 1 - 1) * (taylorB β σ κ φπ φx 1 0 / (2 * (c + 1))) =
      -(c * taylorB β σ κ φπ φx 1 0 / (2 * (c + 1))) := by rw [hc]; ring
  rw [hxe]
  have : c * taylorB β σ κ φπ φx 1 0 / (2 * (c + 1)) < taylorB β σ κ φπ φx 1 0 := by
    rw [div_lt_iff₀ (by positivity)]
    nlinarith
  linarith

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 268: a line `a p + b x = 0` with `(a, b) ≠ 0` in the `(xᵉ, πᵉ)` plane is
the set of multiples of the direction `(x, p) = (a, −b)`. -/
theorem line_iff {a b : ℝ} (hab : a ≠ 0 ∨ b ≠ 0) (p x : ℝ) :
    a * p + b * x = 0 ↔ ∃ c : ℝ, x = c * a ∧ p = c * -b := by
  constructor
  · intro h
    rcases hab with ha | hb
    · exact ⟨x / a, by field_simp, by field_simp; linarith⟩
    · refine ⟨-p / b, ?_, by field_simp⟩
      field_simp
      linear_combination h
  · rintro ⟨c, rfl, rfl⟩
    ring

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 268: the entries of `B` used by the phase diagrams. -/
theorem taylorB01 : taylorB β σ κ φπ φx 0 1 = κ / taylorDelta σ κ φπ φx := rfl

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 268: the entry `B₁₀ = σ(1 − βφ_π)/Δ`. -/
theorem taylorB10 : taylorB β σ κ φπ φx 1 0 = σ * (1 - β * φπ) / taylorDelta σ κ φπ φx := rfl

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 268: the cross product `d₁ d′₂ − d₂ d′₁` of a direction `d` of a line
through the origin with its derivative `d′`; it equals `|d|²` times the rate of change of the
line's angle, so it is negative for clockwise and positive for counterclockwise rotation
(unchanged if `d` is rescaled by a positive factor or reversed). -/
def cross (d d' : ℝ × ℝ) : ℝ := d.1 * d'.2 - d.2 * d'.1

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 268: a direction `(xᵉ, πᵉ)` of the `π̇ᵉ = 0` locus,
`(N, −κ)` with `N = κσ(1 − φ_π) − (1 − β)(1 + σφ_x/4)`. -/
noncomputable def piDir (β κ σ φπ φx : ℝ) : ℝ × ℝ :=
  (κ * σ * (1 - φπ) - (1 - β) * (1 + σ * φx / 4), -κ)

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 268: a direction `(xᵉ, πᵉ)` of the `ẋᵉ = 0` locus,
`(1 − βφ_π, φ_x/4 + κφ_π)`. -/
noncomputable def xDir (β κ φπ φx : ℝ) : ℝ × ℝ := (1 - β * φπ, φx / 4 + κ * φπ)

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 268: the `π̇ᵉ = 0` locus is the line through the origin spanned by
`piDir`. -/
theorem piDot_eq_zero_iff (hκ : 0 < κ) (hσ : 0 < σ) (hπ : 0 ≤ φπ) (hx : 0 ≤ φx) (pe xe : ℝ) :
    piDot β κ σ φπ φx pe xe = 0 ↔
      ∃ c : ℝ, xe = c * (piDir β κ σ φπ φx).1 ∧ pe = c * (piDir β κ σ φπ φx).2 := by
  have hD := taylorDelta_pos hσ hκ hπ hx
  have h : piDot β κ σ φπ φx pe xe =
      ((κ * σ * (1 - φπ) - (1 - β) * (1 + σ * φx / 4)) * pe + κ * xe) / taylorDelta σ κ φπ φx := by
    rw [piDot, taylorB00_sub_one hD.ne', taylorB01]
    ring
  rw [h, div_eq_zero_iff, or_iff_left hD.ne', line_iff (Or.inr hκ.ne')]
  simp only [piDir]

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 268: the `ẋᵉ = 0` locus is the line through the origin spanned by
`xDir`. -/
theorem xDot_eq_zero_iff (hκ : 0 < κ) (hσ : 0 < σ) (hπ : 0 ≤ φπ) (hx : 0 ≤ φx) (pe xe : ℝ) :
    xDot β κ σ φπ φx pe xe = 0 ↔
      ∃ c : ℝ, xe = c * (xDir β κ φπ φx).1 ∧ pe = c * (xDir β κ φπ φx).2 := by
  have hD := taylorDelta_pos hσ hκ hπ hx
  have h : xDot β κ σ φπ φx pe xe =
      σ * ((1 - β * φπ) * pe + -(φx / 4 + κ * φπ) * xe) / taylorDelta σ κ φπ φx := by
    rw [xDot, taylorB11_sub_one hD.ne', taylorB10]
    ring
  have hab : 1 - β * φπ ≠ 0 ∨ -(φx / 4 + κ * φπ) ≠ 0 := by
    by_cases h1 : 1 - β * φπ = 0
    · right
      have : φπ ≠ 0 := by rintro rfl; simp at h1
      have : 0 < κ * φπ := mul_pos hκ (lt_of_le_of_ne hπ (Ne.symm this))
      have : 0 < φx / 4 + κ * φπ := by positivity
      exact neg_ne_zero.mpr this.ne'
    · exact Or.inl h1
  rw [h, div_eq_zero_iff, or_iff_left hD.ne', mul_eq_zero, or_iff_right hσ.ne',
    line_iff hab]
  simp only [xDir, neg_neg]

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 268: **increasing `φ_π` rotates the `π̇ᵉ = 0` locus clockwise**: the
direction has derivative `(−κσ, 0)` in `φ_π` and the cross product is `−κ²σ < 0`. -/
theorem piLocus_rotates_clockwise_phiPi (hκ : 0 < κ) (hσ : 0 < σ) :
    HasDerivAt (fun q => (piDir β κ σ q φx).1) (-(κ * σ)) φπ ∧
      HasDerivAt (fun q => (piDir β κ σ q φx).2) 0 φπ ∧
      cross (piDir β κ σ φπ φx) (-(κ * σ), 0) < 0 := by
  refine ⟨?_, hasDerivAt_const _ _, ?_⟩
  · have h : (fun q => (piDir β κ σ q φx).1) =
        fun q => -(κ * σ) * q + (κ * σ - (1 - β) * (1 + σ * φx / 4)) := by
      funext q; simp only [piDir]; ring
    rw [h]
    simpa using ((hasDerivAt_id φπ).const_mul (-(κ * σ))).add_const
      (κ * σ - (1 - β) * (1 + σ * φx / 4))
  · simp only [cross, piDir]
    nlinarith [mul_pos (mul_pos hκ hκ) hσ]

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 268: **increasing `φ_x` rotates the `π̇ᵉ = 0` locus clockwise**: the
direction has derivative `(−(1 − β)σ/4, 0)` in `φ_x` and the cross product is
`−κ(1 − β)σ/4 < 0`. -/
theorem piLocus_rotates_clockwise_phiX (hβ1 : β < 1) (hκ : 0 < κ) (hσ : 0 < σ) :
    HasDerivAt (fun q => (piDir β κ σ φπ q).1) (-((1 - β) * σ / 4)) φx ∧
      HasDerivAt (fun q => (piDir β κ σ φπ q).2) 0 φx ∧
      cross (piDir β κ σ φπ φx) (-((1 - β) * σ / 4), 0) < 0 := by
  refine ⟨?_, hasDerivAt_const _ _, ?_⟩
  · have h : (fun q => (piDir β κ σ φπ q).1) =
        fun q => -((1 - β) * σ / 4) * q + (κ * σ * (1 - φπ) - (1 - β)) := by
      funext q; simp only [piDir]; ring
    rw [h]
    simpa using ((hasDerivAt_id φx).const_mul (-((1 - β) * σ / 4))).add_const
      (κ * σ * (1 - φπ) - (1 - β))
  · simp only [cross, piDir]
    have : 0 < 1 - β := by linarith
    nlinarith [mul_pos (mul_pos hκ this) hσ]

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 268: **increasing `φ_π` rotates the `ẋᵉ = 0` locus counterclockwise**:
the direction has derivative `(−β, κ)` and the cross product is `κ + βφ_x/4 > 0`. -/
theorem xLocus_rotates_counterclockwise_phiPi (hβ0 : 0 < β) (hκ : 0 < κ) (hx : 0 ≤ φx) :
    HasDerivAt (fun q => (xDir β κ q φx).1) (-β) φπ ∧
      HasDerivAt (fun q => (xDir β κ q φx).2) κ φπ ∧
      0 < cross (xDir β κ φπ φx) (-β, κ) := by
  refine ⟨?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · have h : (fun q => (xDir β κ q φx).1) = fun q => -β * q + 1 := by
      funext q; simp only [xDir]; ring
    rw [h]
    simpa using ((hasDerivAt_id φπ).const_mul (-β)).add_const 1
  · have h : (fun q => (xDir β κ q φx).2) = fun q => κ * q + φx / 4 := by
      funext q; simp only [xDir]; ring
    rw [h]
    simpa using ((hasDerivAt_id φπ).const_mul κ).add_const (φx / 4)
  · simp only [cross, xDir]
    nlinarith [mul_nonneg hβ0.le hx]

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 268 (imprecision): increasing `φ_x` rotates the `ẋᵉ = 0` locus with
cross product `(1 − βφ_π)/4`: **counterclockwise iff `φ_π < β⁻¹`** (the case drawn in Figure 4.4,
footnote 39), clockwise when `φ_π > β⁻¹`. The book states the counterclockwise rotation without
this proviso. -/
theorem xLocus_rotation_phiX (hβ0 : 0 < β) :
    HasDerivAt (fun q => (xDir β κ φπ q).1) 0 φx ∧
      HasDerivAt (fun q => (xDir β κ φπ q).2) (1 / 4) φx ∧
      (0 < cross (xDir β κ φπ φx) (0, 1 / 4) ↔ φπ < β⁻¹) := by
  refine ⟨hasDerivAt_const _ _, ?_, ?_⟩
  · have h : (fun q => (xDir β κ φπ q).2) = fun q => 1 / 4 * q + κ * φπ := by
      funext q; simp only [xDir]; ring
    rw [h]
    simpa using ((hasDerivAt_id φx).const_mul (1 / 4 : ℝ)).add_const (κ * φπ)
  · simp only [cross, xDir, mul_zero, sub_zero]
    constructor
    · intro h
      have h2 : φπ = β⁻¹ * (β * φπ) := by field_simp
      rw [h2]
      have : β * φπ < 1 := by linarith
      calc β⁻¹ * (β * φπ) < β⁻¹ * 1 := mul_lt_mul_of_pos_left this (inv_pos.mpr hβ0)
        _ = β⁻¹ := mul_one _
    · intro h
      have h3 := mul_lt_mul_of_pos_left h hβ0
      rw [mul_inv_cancel₀ hβ0.ne'] at h3
      linarith

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 268: `(B₀₀ − 1)(B₁₁ − 1) − B₀₁B₁₀ = det(B − I) = 1 − tr B + det B`. -/
theorem det_taylorB_sub_one_entries :
    (taylorB β σ κ φπ φx 0 0 - 1) * (taylorB β σ κ φπ φx 1 1 - 1) -
        taylorB β σ κ φπ φx 0 1 * taylorB β σ κ φπ φx 1 0 =
      1 - tr2 (taylorB β σ κ φπ φx) + det2 (taylorB β σ κ φπ φx) := by
  simp only [tr2, det2]
  ring

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 268: **the `π̇ᵉ = 0` and `ẋᵉ = 0` loci coincide iff (2.7) holds with
equality**. -/
theorem loci_coincide_iff (hκ : 0 < κ) (hσ : 0 < σ) (hπ : 0 ≤ φπ) (hx : 0 ≤ φx) :
    (∀ pe xe, piDot β κ σ φπ φx pe xe = 0 ↔ xDot β κ σ φπ φx pe xe = 0) ↔
      taylorLHS β κ φπ φx = 1 := by
  have hD := taylorDelta_pos hσ hκ hπ hx
  have hkey : 1 - tr2 (taylorB β σ κ φπ φx) + det2 (taylorB β σ κ φπ φx) =
      κ * σ * (taylorLHS β κ φπ φx - 1) / taylorDelta σ κ φπ φx := by
    linear_combination taylorB_one_sub (β := β) (φπ := φπ) (φx := φx) hκ.ne' hD.ne'
  have hdet := det_taylorB_sub_one_entries (β := β) (κ := κ) (σ := σ) (φπ := φπ) (φx := φx)
  have h01 : taylorB β σ κ φπ φx 0 1 ≠ 0 := by rw [taylorB01]; exact (div_pos hκ hD).ne'
  constructor
  · intro h
    have h1 : piDot β κ σ φπ φx (taylorB β σ κ φπ φx 0 1) (1 - taylorB β σ κ φπ φx 0 0) = 0 := by
      unfold piDot; ring
    have h2 := (h _ _).mp h1
    unfold xDot at h2
    have h3 : κ * σ * (taylorLHS β κ φπ φx - 1) / taylorDelta σ κ φπ φx = 0 := by
      rw [← hkey, ← hdet]; linear_combination -h2
    rcases div_eq_zero_iff.mp h3 with h4 | h4
    · rcases mul_eq_zero.mp h4 with h5 | h5
      · exact absurd h5 (mul_pos hκ hσ).ne'
      · linarith
    · exact absurd h4 hD.ne'
  · intro hT pe xe
    have hd0 : (taylorB β σ κ φπ φx 0 0 - 1) * (taylorB β σ κ φπ φx 1 1 - 1) -
        taylorB β σ κ φπ φx 0 1 * taylorB β σ κ φπ φx 1 0 = 0 := by
      rw [hdet, hkey, hT, sub_self, mul_zero, zero_div]
    have h11 : taylorB β σ κ φπ φx 1 1 - 1 ≠ 0 := by
      rw [taylorB11_sub_one hD.ne']
      refine div_ne_zero (neg_ne_zero.mpr ?_) hD.ne'
      refine mul_ne_zero hσ.ne' ?_
      intro h0
      have hπ0 : φπ = 0 := by nlinarith [mul_nonneg hκ.le hπ]
      have hx0 : φx = 0 := by nlinarith [mul_nonneg hκ.le hπ]
      rw [taylorLHS, hπ0, hx0] at hT
      simp at hT
    set c := (taylorB β σ κ φπ φx 1 1 - 1) / taylorB β σ κ φπ φx 0 1 with hc
    have hc0 : c ≠ 0 := div_ne_zero h11 h01
    have hrel : xDot β κ σ φπ φx pe xe = c * piDot β κ σ φπ φx pe xe := by
      unfold xDot piDot
      rw [hc]
      field_simp
      linear_combination (-pe) * hd0
    rw [hrel, mul_eq_zero, or_iff_right hc0]

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 264 (footnote 35) and p. 268: the steady states `z = z̄ + B(z − z̄)`
(equivalently, the self-consistent sample-mean beliefs and the intercepts of the s.c.e.) form
an **infinite set (a continuum) iff (2.7) holds with equality**; otherwise `z̄` is the only
one. -/
theorem steadyStates_infinite_iff (hκ : 0 < κ) (hσ : 0 < σ) (hπ : 0 ≤ φπ) (hx : 0 ≤ φx)
    (zbar : Fin 2 → ℝ) :
    {z | Tmap (taylorB β σ κ φπ φx) zbar z = z}.Infinite ↔
      taylorLHS β κ φπ φx = 1 := by
  have hD := taylorDelta_pos hσ hκ hπ hx
  have hkey : 1 - tr2 (taylorB β σ κ φπ φx) + det2 (taylorB β σ κ φπ φx) =
      κ * σ * (taylorLHS β κ φπ φx - 1) / taylorDelta σ κ φπ φx := by
    linear_combination taylorB_one_sub (β := β) (φπ := φπ) (φx := φx) hκ.ne' hD.ne'
  constructor
  · intro hinf
    by_contra hT
    have hB : (1 - taylorB β σ κ φπ φx).det ≠ 0 := by
      rw [det_one_sub_taylorB, hkey]
      refine div_ne_zero (mul_ne_zero (mul_pos hκ hσ).ne' (sub_ne_zero.mpr hT)) hD.ne'
    apply hinf
    refine (Set.finite_singleton zbar).subset fun z hz => ?_
    exact (Tmap_fixed_unique _ zbar hB z).mp hz
  · intro hT
    have hd0 : 1 - tr2 (taylorB β σ κ φπ φx) + det2 (taylorB β σ κ φπ φx) = 0 := by
      rw [hkey, hT, sub_self, mul_zero, zero_div]
    set w : Fin 2 → ℝ := ![taylorB β σ κ φπ φx 0 1, 1 - taylorB β σ κ φπ φx 0 0] with hw
    have hw0 : w 0 ≠ 0 := by
      simp only [hw, cons_val_zero, taylorB01]; exact (div_pos hκ hD).ne'
    have hker : (1 - taylorB β σ κ φπ φx) *ᵥ w = 0 := by
      funext i
      fin_cases i
      · simp [hw, mulVec, dotProduct, Fin.sum_univ_two]; ring
      · simp [hw, mulVec, dotProduct, Fin.sum_univ_two]
        simp only [tr2, det2] at hd0
        linear_combination hd0
    refine Set.infinite_of_injective_forall_mem (f := fun c : ℝ => zbar + c • w) ?_ ?_
    · intro c₁ c₂ h
      have := congrFun h 0
      simp only [Pi.add_apply, Pi.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul, add_right_inj] at this
      exact mul_right_cancel₀ hw0 this
    · intro c
      change Tmap _ zbar (zbar + c • w) = zbar + c • w
      rw [Tmap_fixed_iff_one_sub, add_sub_cancel_left, mulVec_smul, hker, smul_zero]

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 268: at equality in (2.7) every eigenvalue of `B` has modulus at most
one (they are `1` and `det B = β/Δ`). -/
theorem norm_le_one_of_isEig_taylorB_of_eq (hβ0 : 0 < β) (hβ1 : β < 1) (hκ : 0 < κ) (hσ : 0 < σ)
    (hπ : 0 ≤ φπ) (hx : 0 ≤ φx) (hT : taylorLHS β κ φπ φx = 1) {μ : ℂ}
    (h : KroneckerSpectrum.IsEig ((taylorB β σ κ φπ φx).map Complex.ofReal) μ) : ‖μ‖ ≤ 1 := by
  have hD := taylorDelta_pos hσ hκ hπ hx
  have hD1 := one_le_taylorDelta hσ hκ hπ hx
  have hkey : 1 - tr2 (taylorB β σ κ φπ φx) + det2 (taylorB β σ κ φπ φx) =
      κ * σ * (taylorLHS β κ φπ φx - 1) / taylorDelta σ κ φπ φx := by
    linear_combination taylorB_one_sub (β := β) (φπ := φπ) (φx := φx) hκ.ne' hD.ne'
  have hd0 : tr2 (taylorB β σ κ φπ φx) = 1 + det2 (taylorB β σ κ φπ φx) := by
    rw [hT, sub_self, mul_zero, zero_div] at hkey; linarith
  have hdet := taylorB_det (β := β) hD.ne'
  have hdet0 : 0 < det2 (taylorB β σ κ φπ φx) := by rw [hdet]; positivity
  have hdet1 : det2 (taylorB β σ κ φπ φx) < 1 := by rw [hdet, div_lt_one hD]; linarith
  have hμ := (isEig_two_iff _ μ).mp h
  rw [hd0] at hμ
  push_cast at hμ
  have hf : (μ - 1) * (μ - (det2 (taylorB β σ κ φπ φx) : ℂ)) = 0 := by linear_combination hμ
  rcases mul_eq_zero.mp hf with h1 | h1
  · rw [sub_eq_zero.mp h1, norm_one]
  · rw [sub_eq_zero.mp h1, Complex.norm_real, Real.norm_eq_abs, abs_of_pos hdet0]
    exact hdet1.le

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 268 (regression version): at equality in (2.7), with a stationary state,
the regression `T`-map has a continuum of fixed points (s.c.e.): infinitely many. -/
theorem fixed_infinite_of_eq (hβ0 : 0 < β) (hβ1 : β < 1) (hκ : 0 < κ) (hσ : 0 < σ)
    (hπ : 0 ≤ φπ) (hx : 0 ≤ φx) (hT : taylorLHS β κ φπ φx = 1) (zbar : Fin 2 → ℝ)
    (g : S → ℝ) (C : Matrix S S ℝ)
    (hC : ∀ ρ, KroneckerSpectrum.IsEig (C.map Complex.ofReal) ρ → ‖ρ‖ < 1) :
    {Φ : Belief (Fin 2) S |
      tMap zbar (taylorB β σ κ φπ φx) (taylorb σ κ φπ φx) g C Φ = Φ}.Infinite := by
  obtain ⟨X, hX, -⟩ := sylvester_existsUnique (taylorB β σ κ φπ φx) C
    (vecMulVec (taylorb σ κ φπ φx) g * C) (not_isEig_one_kronecker hC
      fun l hl => norm_le_one_of_isEig_taylorB_of_eq hβ0 hβ1 hκ hσ hπ hx hT hl)
  have hinf := (steadyStates_infinite_iff (β := β) hκ hσ hπ hx zbar).mpr hT
  obtain ⟨f, hf, hfmem⟩ : ∃ f : ℕ → Fin 2 → ℝ, Function.Injective f ∧
      ∀ k, Tmap (taylorB β σ κ φπ φx) zbar (f k) = f k := by
    obtain ⟨f, hf⟩ := hinf.natEmbedding
    exact ⟨fun k => (f k).1, fun a b h => hf (Subtype.ext h), fun k => (f k).2⟩
  refine Set.infinite_of_injective_forall_mem (f := fun k => ((f k, X) : Belief (Fin 2) S))
    (fun a b h => hf (congrArg Prod.fst h)) fun k => ?_
  change tMap zbar _ _ g C (f k, X) = (f k, X)
  rw [tMap_fixed_iff]
  exact ⟨(Tmap_fixed_iff_one_sub _ zbar _).mp (hfmem k), hX⟩

end BullardMitra

/-! ### Preston's long-horizon forms (2.28)–(2.30) -/

namespace Preston

variable {Ω : Type*} (𝔼 : ExpectationSystem Ω)

/-- Woodford (2003), pp. 273–274: for `0 ≤ a < 1` and bounded processes, the long-horizon form
`z_t = E_t ∑_{k ≥ 0} aᵏ w_{t+k}` holds at every date iff the one-step form
`z_t = a E_t z_{t+1} + E_t w_t` does (the tower property links the two). -/
theorem forward_iff {a : ℝ} (ha0 : 0 ≤ a) (ha1 : a < 1) {w z : ℕ → Ω → ℝ}
    (hw : ∃ M, ∀ t ω, |w t ω| ≤ M) (hz : BoundedProc z) :
    (∀ t, z t = 𝔼.E t (fun ω => ∑' k, a ^ k * w (t + k) ω)) ↔
      ∀ t, z t = a • 𝔼.E t (z (t + 1)) + 𝔼.E t (w t) := by
  obtain ⟨M, hM⟩ := hw
  have hsum : ∀ t ω, Summable fun k => a ^ k * w (t + k) ω := fun t ω => by
    refine Summable.of_norm_bounded ((summable_geometric_of_lt_one ha0 ha1).mul_right M)
      fun k => ?_
    rw [Real.norm_eq_abs, abs_mul, abs_pow, abs_of_nonneg ha0]
    exact mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left (hM (t + k) ω) (pow_nonneg ha0 k)
  constructor
  · intro h t
    have hsplit : (fun ω => ∑' k, a ^ k * w (t + k) ω) =
        w t + a • fun ω => ∑' k, a ^ k * w (t + 1 + k) ω := by
      funext ω
      rw [(hsum t ω).tsum_eq_zero_add, pow_zero, one_mul, add_zero, Pi.add_apply,
        Pi.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul, ← tsum_mul_left]
      congr 1
      refine tsum_congr fun k => ?_
      rw [show t + (k + 1) = t + 1 + k by omega, pow_succ]
      ring
    have h1 : 𝔼.E t (fun ω => ∑' k, a ^ k * w (t + 1 + k) ω) = 𝔼.E t (z (t + 1)) := by
      rw [h (t + 1), 𝔼.tower (Nat.le_succ t)]
    rw [h t, hsplit, map_add, map_smul, h1, add_comm]
  · intro h
    set u : ℕ → Ω → ℝ := fun t => 𝔼.E t (w t) with hu
    have hub : ∀ t ω, |u t ω| ≤ M := fun t ω => 𝔼.abs_E_le (hM t) t ω
    have hua : 𝔼.Adapted u := fun t => 𝔼.E_E_self t (w t)
    have hz' : ∀ t, z t = a • 𝔼.E t (z (t + 1)) + u t := h
    have heq := 𝔼.eq_forwardSeries ha0 ha1 hub hua hz' hz
    intro t
    rw [heq]
    funext ω
    have hb : ∀ k ω', |a ^ k * w (t + k) ω'| ≤ a ^ k * M := fun k ω' => by
      rw [abs_mul, abs_pow, abs_of_nonneg ha0]
      exact mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left (hM (t + k) ω') (pow_nonneg ha0 k)
    rw [𝔼.E_tsum ha0 ha1 hb t ω]
    refine tsum_congr fun k => ?_
    have hf : (fun ω' => a ^ k * w (t + k) ω') = a ^ k • w (t + k) := by
      funext ω'; simp
    rw [hf, map_smul, hu, 𝔼.tower (Nat.le_add_right t k)]
    rfl

/-- Woodford (2003), (2.29) p. 273: Preston's long-horizon aggregate-demand relation
`x_t = Ê_t ∑_{T ≥ t} β^{T−t}[(1 − β)x_{T+1} − σ(î_T − π_{T+1} − r̂ⁿ_T)]`, with the expectation
operator `Ê`. -/
def PrestonIS {Ω : Type*} (Ehat : ℕ → (Ω → ℝ) →ₗ[ℝ] (Ω → ℝ)) (β σ : ℝ)
    (x infl i rn : ℕ → Ω → ℝ) : Prop :=
  ∀ t, x t = Ehat t (fun ω => ∑' k, β ^ k *
    ((1 - β) * x (t + k + 1) ω - σ * (i (t + k) ω - infl (t + k + 1) ω - rn (t + k) ω)))

/-- Woodford (2003), (2.17) p. 263: the one-period-ahead IS relation with expectations `Ê`. -/
def OneStepIS {Ω : Type*} (Ehat : ℕ → (Ω → ℝ) →ₗ[ℝ] (Ω → ℝ)) (σ : ℝ)
    (x infl i rn : ℕ → Ω → ℝ) : Prop :=
  ∀ t, x t = Ehat t (x (t + 1)) - σ • (i t - Ehat t (infl (t + 1)) - rn t)

/-- Woodford (2003), (2.30) p. 273: Preston's long-horizon inflation equation
`π_t = Ê_t ∑_{T ≥ t} (αβ)^{T−t}[κ x_T + (1 − α)β π_{T+1}]`. -/
def PrestonAS {Ω : Type*} (Ehat : ℕ → (Ω → ℝ) →ₗ[ℝ] (Ω → ℝ)) (α β κ : ℝ)
    (x infl : ℕ → Ω → ℝ) : Prop :=
  ∀ t, infl t = Ehat t (fun ω => ∑' k, (α * β) ^ k *
    (κ * x (t + k) ω + (1 - α) * β * infl (t + k + 1) ω))

/-- Woodford (2003), (2.16) p. 263: the one-period-ahead Phillips curve with expectations
`Ê`. -/
def OneStepAS {Ω : Type*} (Ehat : ℕ → (Ω → ℝ) →ₗ[ℝ] (Ω → ℝ)) (β κ : ℝ)
    (x infl : ℕ → Ω → ℝ) : Prop :=
  ∀ t, infl t = κ • x t + β • Ehat t (infl (t + 1))

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 273: **under rational expectations (2.29) ⟺ (2.17)**, for bounded
processes with `î`, `r̂ⁿ` known at their dates, `0 < β < 1`, and any `ExpectationSystem`. -/
theorem preston_IS_iff {β σ : ℝ} (hβ0 : 0 < β) (hβ1 : β < 1) {x infl i rn : ℕ → Ω → ℝ}
    (hx : BoundedProc x) (hπ : BoundedProc infl) (hi : BoundedProc i) (hr : BoundedProc rn)
    (hia : 𝔼.Adapted i) (hra : 𝔼.Adapted rn) :
    PrestonIS 𝔼.E β σ x infl i rn ↔ OneStepIS 𝔼.E σ x infl i rn := by
  set w : ℕ → Ω → ℝ := fun T ω =>
    (1 - β) * x (T + 1) ω - σ * (i T ω - infl (T + 1) ω - rn T ω) with hw
  have hwb : ∃ M, ∀ t ω, |w t ω| ≤ M := by
    obtain ⟨Mx, hMx⟩ := hx
    obtain ⟨Mπ, hMπ⟩ := hπ
    obtain ⟨Mi, hMi⟩ := hi
    obtain ⟨Mr, hMr⟩ := hr
    refine ⟨|1 - β| * Mx + |σ| * (Mi + Mπ + Mr), fun t ω => ?_⟩
    simp only [hw]
    refine (abs_sub _ _).trans (add_le_add ?_ ?_)
    · rw [abs_mul]
      exact mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left (hMx _ _) (abs_nonneg _)
    · rw [abs_mul]
      refine mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left ?_ (abs_nonneg _)
      refine (abs_sub _ _).trans (add_le_add ((abs_sub _ _).trans
        (add_le_add (hMi _ _) (hMπ _ _))) (hMr _ _))
  have hlong : PrestonIS 𝔼.E β σ x infl i rn ↔
      ∀ t, x t = 𝔼.E t (fun ω => ∑' k, β ^ k * w (t + k) ω) := by
    refine forall_congr' fun t => ?_
    simp only [hw]
  have hEw : ∀ t, 𝔼.E t (w t) =
      (1 - β) • 𝔼.E t (x (t + 1)) - σ • (i t - 𝔼.E t (infl (t + 1)) - rn t) := by
    intro t
    have : w t = (1 - β) • x (t + 1) - σ • (i t - infl (t + 1) - rn t) := by
      funext ω; simp [hw]
    rw [this, map_sub, map_smul, map_smul, map_sub, map_sub, hia t, hra t]
  rw [hlong, forward_iff 𝔼 hβ0.le hβ1 hwb hx]
  refine forall_congr' fun t => ?_
  rw [hEw]
  constructor <;> intro h <;> rw [h] <;> module

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 274: **under rational expectations (2.30) ⟺ (2.16)**, for bounded
processes with `x` known at its date, `0 ≤ α < 1`, `0 < β < 1`, and any `ExpectationSystem`. -/
theorem preston_AS_iff {α β κ : ℝ} (hα0 : 0 ≤ α) (hα1 : α < 1) (hβ0 : 0 < β) (hβ1 : β < 1)
    {x infl : ℕ → Ω → ℝ} (hx : BoundedProc x) (hπ : BoundedProc infl) (hxa : 𝔼.Adapted x) :
    PrestonAS 𝔼.E α β κ x infl ↔ OneStepAS 𝔼.E β κ x infl := by
  set w : ℕ → Ω → ℝ := fun T ω => κ * x T ω + (1 - α) * β * infl (T + 1) ω with hw
  have hwb : ∃ M, ∀ t ω, |w t ω| ≤ M := by
    obtain ⟨Mx, hMx⟩ := hx
    obtain ⟨Mπ, hMπ⟩ := hπ
    refine ⟨|κ| * Mx + |(1 - α) * β| * Mπ, fun t ω => ?_⟩
    simp only [hw]
    refine (abs_add_le _ _).trans (add_le_add ?_ ?_)
    · rw [abs_mul]
      exact mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left (hMx _ _) (abs_nonneg _)
    · rw [abs_mul]
      exact mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left (hMπ _ _) (abs_nonneg _)
  have hlong : PrestonAS 𝔼.E α β κ x infl ↔
      ∀ t, infl t = 𝔼.E t (fun ω => ∑' k, (α * β) ^ k * w (t + k) ω) := by
    refine forall_congr' fun t => ?_
    simp only [hw]
  have hEw : ∀ t, 𝔼.E t (w t) = κ • x t + ((1 - α) * β) • 𝔼.E t (infl (t + 1)) := by
    intro t
    have : w t = κ • x t + ((1 - α) * β) • infl (t + 1) := by
      funext ω; simp [hw]
    rw [this, map_add, map_smul, map_smul, hxa t]
  have hab0 : 0 ≤ α * β := mul_nonneg hα0 hβ0.le
  have hab1 : α * β < 1 := by nlinarith
  rw [hlong, forward_iff 𝔼 hab0 hab1 hwb hπ]
  refine forall_congr' fun t => ?_
  rw [hEw]
  constructor <;> intro h <;> rw [h] <;> module

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 273: under general forecasting rules (2.29) does **not** imply (2.17):
with forecasts identically zero (a linear forecasting rule that is not an `ExpectationSystem`),
`x = π = r̂ⁿ = 0`, `î = 1`, (2.29) holds and (2.17) fails, for any `β` and any `σ ≠ 0`. -/
theorem preston_IS_not_imp (β : ℝ) {σ : ℝ} (hσ : σ ≠ 0) :
    PrestonIS (fun _ => (0 : (Unit → ℝ) →ₗ[ℝ] (Unit → ℝ))) β σ 0 0 1 0 ∧
      ¬ OneStepIS (fun _ => (0 : (Unit → ℝ) →ₗ[ℝ] (Unit → ℝ))) σ 0 0 1 0 := by
  refine ⟨fun t => by simp, fun h => ?_⟩
  have := congrFun (h 0) ()
  exact hσ (by simpa using this)

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 273: under general forecasting rules (2.17) does **not** imply (2.29):
with zero forecasts, `x = −σ`, `π = r̂ⁿ = 0`, `î = 1`, (2.17) holds and (2.29) fails. -/
theorem preston_IS_not_imp' (β : ℝ) {σ : ℝ} (hσ : σ ≠ 0) :
    OneStepIS (fun _ => (0 : (Unit → ℝ) →ₗ[ℝ] (Unit → ℝ))) σ (fun _ _ => -σ) 0 1 0 ∧
      ¬ PrestonIS (fun _ => (0 : (Unit → ℝ) →ₗ[ℝ] (Unit → ℝ))) β σ (fun _ _ => -σ) 0 1 0 := by
  refine ⟨fun t => by funext ω; simp, fun h => ?_⟩
  have := congrFun (h 0) ()
  exact hσ (by simpa using this)

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 273: the average private-sector forecast `Ê_t[·] ≡ ∫ Êⁱ_t[·] di` over a
probability space of agents with arbitrary (linear) subjective expectations `Êⁱ`. -/
noncomputable def avgE {I : Type*} [MeasurableSpace I] (μ : MeasureTheory.Measure I)
    (Ehat : I → ℕ → (Ω → ℝ) →ₗ[ℝ] (Ω → ℝ)) (t : ℕ) (X : Ω → ℝ) : Ω → ℝ :=
  fun ω => ∫ j, Ehat j t X ω ∂μ

/-- Woodford (2003), (2.28) p. 272: the long-horizon sum in the household spending rule,
`∑ β^{T−t}[(1 − β)s_C⁻¹(Ŷ_T − G_T) − (1 − β)C̄_T − βσ̃(î_T − π_{T+1})]`. -/
noncomputable def spendSeries (β sC σt : ℝ) (Y G Cbar i infl : ℕ → Ω → ℝ) (t : ℕ) : Ω → ℝ :=
  fun ω => ∑' k, β ^ k * ((1 - β) / sC * (Y (t + k) ω - G (t + k) ω) -
    (1 - β) * Cbar (t + k) ω - β * σt * (i (t + k) ω - infl (t + k + 1) ω))

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 273: the long-horizon sum of the aggregate-demand relation,
`∑ β^{T−t}[(1 − β)(Ŷ_T − g_T) − βσ(î_T − π_{T+1})]`. -/
noncomputable def demandSeries (β σ : ℝ) (Y g i infl : ℕ → Ω → ℝ) (t : ℕ) : Ω → ℝ :=
  fun ω => ∑' k, β ^ k * ((1 - β) * (Y (t + k) ω - g (t + k) ω) -
    β * σ * (i (t + k) ω - infl (t + k + 1) ω))

/-- Woodford (2003), (2.28) and p. 273: **aggregating Preston's household spending rule.** If
every household `j` spends according to (2.28) under its own linear subjective expectations,
aggregate demand is `Ŷ_t = s_C ∫ Ĉʲ_t dj + Ĝ_t`, and net wealth integrates to zero, then
`Ŷ_t = g_t + Ê_t ∑ β^{T−t}[(1 − β)(Ŷ_T − g_T) − βσ(î_T − π_{T+1})]` with `g = Ĝ + s_C C̄`,
`σ = s_C σ̃` and `Ê` the average forecast (integrability of the household terms assumed). -/
theorem aggregate_demand {I : Type*} [MeasurableSpace I] (μ : MeasureTheory.Measure I)
    [MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure μ] (Ehat : I → ℕ → (Ω → ℝ) →ₗ[ℝ] (Ω → ℝ))
    {β sC σt : ℝ} (hsC : sC ≠ 0) (C W : I → ℕ → Ω → ℝ) (Cbar Y G i infl : ℕ → Ω → ℝ)
    (hrule : ∀ j t, C j t = Cbar t + ((1 - β) / sC) • W j t +
      Ehat j t (spendSeries β sC σt Y G Cbar i infl t))
    (hY : ∀ t ω, Y t ω = sC * ∫ j, C j t ω ∂μ + G t ω)
    (hW : ∀ t ω, ∫ j, W j t ω ∂μ = 0)
    (hWi : ∀ t ω, MeasureTheory.Integrable (fun j => W j t ω) μ)
    (hEi : ∀ t ω, MeasureTheory.Integrable
      (fun j => Ehat j t (spendSeries β sC σt Y G Cbar i infl t) ω) μ) (t : ℕ) :
    Y t = (G t + sC • Cbar t) +
      avgE μ Ehat t (demandSeries β (sC * σt) Y (fun T => G T + sC • Cbar T) i infl t) := by
  have hser : demandSeries β (sC * σt) Y (fun T => G T + sC • Cbar T) i infl t =
      sC • spendSeries β sC σt Y G Cbar i infl t := by
    funext ω
    simp only [demandSeries, spendSeries, Pi.smul_apply, Pi.add_apply, smul_eq_mul,
      ← tsum_mul_left]
    refine tsum_congr fun k => ?_
    field_simp
    ring
  funext ω
  have hC : ∫ j, C j t ω ∂μ =
      Cbar t ω + ∫ j, Ehat j t (spendSeries β sC σt Y G Cbar i infl t) ω ∂μ := by
    have h1 : (fun j => C j t ω) = fun j => (Cbar t ω + (1 - β) / sC * W j t ω) +
        Ehat j t (spendSeries β sC σt Y G Cbar i infl t) ω := by
      funext j
      rw [hrule j t]
      simp
    have hA : MeasureTheory.Integrable (fun j => Cbar t ω + (1 - β) / sC * W j t ω) μ :=
      (MeasureTheory.integrable_const _).add ((hWi t ω).const_mul _)
    rw [h1, MeasureTheory.integral_add hA (hEi t ω),
      MeasureTheory.integral_add (f := fun _ => Cbar t ω)
        (g := fun j => (1 - β) / sC * W j t ω) (MeasureTheory.integrable_const _)
        ((hWi t ω).const_mul _),
      MeasureTheory.integral_const, MeasureTheory.integral_const_mul, hW t ω]
    simp
  rw [hY t ω, hC, hser]
  simp only [avgE, Pi.add_apply, Pi.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul, map_smul,
    MeasureTheory.integral_const_mul]
  ring

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 273: the long-horizon sum in Preston's price-setting rule,
`∑ (αβ)^{T−t}[(1 − αβ)ζ x_T + αβ π_{T+1}]`. -/
noncomputable def priceSeries (α β ζ : ℝ) (x infl : ℕ → Ω → ℝ) (t : ℕ) : Ω → ℝ :=
  fun ω => ∑' k, (α * β) ^ k * ((1 - α * β) * ζ * x (t + k) ω + α * β * infl (t + k + 1) ω)

/-- Woodford (2003), (2.30) p. 273: **aggregating Preston's price-setting rule.** If every
supplier `j` that resets its price chooses `p̂ʲ_t = Êʲ_t ∑ (αβ)^{T−t}[(1 − αβ)ζ x_T + αβ π_{T+1}]`
under its own linear subjective expectations and `π_t = ((1 − α)/α) ∫ p̂ʲ_t dj`, then
`π_t = Ê_t ∑ (αβ)^{T−t}[κ x_T + (1 − α)β π_{T+1}]` with `κ = (1 − α)(1 − αβ)ζ/α`
(`BasicModel.kappa`, the slope of (1.10)) and `Ê` the average forecast (no integrability
assumption needed). -/
theorem aggregate_inflation {J : Type*} [MeasurableSpace J] (μ : MeasureTheory.Measure J)
    (Ehat : J → ℕ → (Ω → ℝ) →ₗ[ℝ] (Ω → ℝ)) {α β ζ : ℝ} (hα : α ≠ 0)
    (p : J → ℕ → Ω → ℝ) (x infl : ℕ → Ω → ℝ)
    (hp : ∀ j t, p j t = Ehat j t (priceSeries α β ζ x infl t))
    (hπ : ∀ t ω, infl t ω = (1 - α) / α * ∫ j, p j t ω ∂μ) (t : ℕ) :
    infl t = avgE μ Ehat t (fun ω => ∑' k, (α * β) ^ k *
      (BasicModel.kappa α β ζ * x (t + k) ω + (1 - α) * β * infl (t + k + 1) ω)) := by
  have hser : (fun ω => ∑' k, (α * β) ^ k *
      (BasicModel.kappa α β ζ * x (t + k) ω + (1 - α) * β * infl (t + k + 1) ω)) =
      ((1 - α) / α) • priceSeries α β ζ x infl t := by
    funext ω
    simp only [priceSeries, Pi.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul, ← tsum_mul_left]
    refine tsum_congr fun k => ?_
    unfold BasicModel.kappa
    field_simp
  funext ω
  rw [hπ t ω, hser]
  simp only [avgE, map_smul, Pi.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul, MeasureTheory.integral_const_mul, hp]

/-- Woodford (2003), footnote 41 (redundant states): without non-degeneracy the converse
`sce_of_rational` fails. With a state identically zero, the belief `Φ = (0, 1)` (slope one on
the redundant state) produces rational forecasts but is not a fixed point of `T`. -/
theorem sce_of_rational_needs_nondegenerate :
    ∃ Φ : Regression.Belief (Fin 2) Unit,
      (∀ t i, Regression.forecast Φ (fun _ _ => (0 : Unit → ℝ)) t i =
        perfectForesight.E t (Regression.dgp 0 0 0 0 Φ (fun _ _ => 0) (t + 1) i)) ∧
      Regression.tMap 0 0 0 0 0 Φ ≠ Φ := by
  refine ⟨(0, fun _ _ => 1), fun t i => ?_, fun h => ?_⟩
  · funext ω
    simp [Regression.forecast, Regression.dgp, Regression.affRV, Regression.dist,
      perfectForesight]
  · have := congrFun (congrFun (congrArg Prod.snd h) 0) ()
    simp [Regression.tMap] at this

/-! #### From the output form of aggregate demand to the gap form (2.29) -/

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 273 (auxiliary): a bounded sequence weighted by `βᵏ`, `0 ≤ β < 1`, is
summable. -/
theorem summable_geom_bdd {β M : ℝ} (hβ0 : 0 ≤ β) (hβ1 : β < 1) {a : ℕ → ℝ}
    (ha : ∀ k, |a k| ≤ M) : Summable fun k => β ^ k * a k := by
  refine Summable.of_norm_bounded ((summable_geometric_of_lt_one hβ0 hβ1).mul_right M)
    fun k => ?_
  rw [Real.norm_eq_abs, abs_mul, abs_pow, abs_of_nonneg hβ0]
  exact mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left (ha k) (pow_nonneg hβ0 k)

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 273 (auxiliary): the telescoping sum
`∑ βᵏ (a_k − β a_{k+1}) = a_0` for a bounded sequence and `0 ≤ β < 1`. -/
theorem tsum_telescope_geom {β M : ℝ} (hβ0 : 0 ≤ β) (hβ1 : β < 1) {a : ℕ → ℝ}
    (ha : ∀ k, |a k| ≤ M) : ∑' k, β ^ k * (a k - β * a (k + 1)) = a 0 := by
  have h1 := summable_geom_bdd hβ0 hβ1 ha
  have h2 : Summable fun k => β ^ (k + 1) * a (k + 1) := (summable_nat_add_iff 1).mpr h1
  have h3 : (fun k => β ^ k * (a k - β * a (k + 1))) =
      fun k => β ^ k * a k - β ^ (k + 1) * a (k + 1) := by
    funext k; ring
  rw [h3, h1.tsum_sub h2, h1.tsum_eq_zero_add]
  simp

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 273: the output form of the aggregate-demand relation,
`Ŷ_t = g_t + Ê_t ∑ β^{T−t}[(1 − β)(Ŷ_T − g_T) − βσ(î_T − π_{T+1})]`. -/
def OutputIS {Ω : Type*} (Ehat : ℕ → (Ω → ℝ) →ₗ[ℝ] (Ω → ℝ)) (β σ : ℝ)
    (Y g i infl : ℕ → Ω → ℝ) : Prop :=
  ∀ t, Y t = g t + Ehat t (demandSeries β σ Y g i infl t)

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 273 and (1.15): the natural-rate series that separates the gap form
from the output form, `∑ β^{T−t}[(1 − β)h_{T+1} + σ r̂ⁿ_T]` with `h = g − Ŷⁿ`. -/
noncomputable def natSeries (β σ : ℝ) (g Yn rn : ℕ → Ω → ℝ) (t : ℕ) : Ω → ℝ :=
  fun ω => ∑' k, β ^ k * ((1 - β) * (g (t + k + 1) ω - Yn (t + k + 1) ω) + σ * rn (t + k) ω)

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 273: **the step from the output form to the gap form (2.29).** For an
arbitrary linear forecasting rule `Ê`, bounded processes, `0 < β < 1`, the output form, and
the implicit assumption that agents know current demand net of `g` (`Ê_t(Ŷ_t − g_t) =
Ŷ_t − g_t`), the gap form (2.29) with `x = Ŷ − Ŷⁿ` holds at every date **iff** the forecasts of
the natural-rate terms are consistent: `Ê_t ∑ β^{T−t}[(1 − β)h_{T+1} + σ r̂ⁿ_T] = h_t`,
`h = g − Ŷⁿ`. This is the minimal assumption the book leaves implicit. -/
theorem gapIS_iff {β σ : ℝ} (hβ0 : 0 < β) (hβ1 : β < 1)
    (Ehat : ℕ → (Ω → ℝ) →ₗ[ℝ] (Ω → ℝ)) {Y g Yn i infl rn : ℕ → Ω → ℝ}
    (hY : BoundedProc Y) (hg : BoundedProc g) (hYn : BoundedProc Yn) (hi : BoundedProc i)
    (hπ : BoundedProc infl) (hr : BoundedProc rn)
    (hout : OutputIS Ehat β σ Y g i infl) (hknown : ∀ t, Ehat t (Y t - g t) = Y t - g t) :
    PrestonIS Ehat β σ (fun t => Y t - Yn t) infl i rn ↔
      ∀ t, Ehat t (natSeries β σ g Yn rn t) = g t - Yn t := by
  obtain ⟨MY, hMY⟩ := hY
  obtain ⟨Mg, hMg⟩ := hg
  obtain ⟨Mn, hMn⟩ := hYn
  obtain ⟨Mi, hMi⟩ := hi
  obtain ⟨Mπ, hMπ⟩ := hπ
  obtain ⟨Mr, hMr⟩ := hr
  have hβ0' := hβ0.le
  -- the one-period-shifted output series `B_t`
  set Bs : ℕ → Ω → ℝ := fun t ω => ∑' k, β ^ k * ((1 - β) * (Y (t + k + 1) ω -
    g (t + k + 1) ω) - σ * (i (t + k) ω - infl (t + k + 1) ω)) with hBs
  have bnd1 : ∀ t ω k, |(1 - β) * (Y (t + k + 1) ω - g (t + k + 1) ω) -
      σ * (i (t + k) ω - infl (t + k + 1) ω)| ≤ |1 - β| * (MY + Mg) + |σ| * (Mi + Mπ) := by
    intro t ω k
    refine (abs_sub _ _).trans (add_le_add ?_ ?_) <;> rw [abs_mul]
    · exact mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left ((abs_sub _ _).trans (add_le_add (hMY _ _) (hMg _ _)))
        (abs_nonneg _)
    · exact mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left ((abs_sub _ _).trans (add_le_add (hMi _ _) (hMπ _ _)))
        (abs_nonneg _)
  have bnd2 : ∀ t ω k, |(1 - β) * (g (t + k + 1) ω - Yn (t + k + 1) ω) + σ * rn (t + k) ω| ≤
      |1 - β| * (Mg + Mn) + |σ| * Mr := by
    intro t ω k
    refine (abs_add_le _ _).trans (add_le_add ?_ ?_) <;> rw [abs_mul]
    · exact mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left ((abs_sub _ _).trans (add_le_add (hMg _ _) (hMn _ _)))
        (abs_nonneg _)
    · exact mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left (hMr _ _) (abs_nonneg _)
  -- (a) the output series splits as `(1 − β)(Ŷ_t − g_t) + β B_t`
  have hsplit : ∀ t, demandSeries β σ Y g i infl t = (1 - β) • (Y t - g t) + β • Bs t := by
    intro t
    funext ω
    set P : ℕ → ℝ := fun k => β ^ k * ((1 - β) * (Y (t + k) ω - g (t + k) ω)) with hP
    set Q : ℕ → ℝ := fun k => β ^ k * (β * σ * (i (t + k) ω - infl (t + k + 1) ω)) with hQ
    have sP : Summable P := by
      refine summable_geom_bdd hβ0' hβ1 (M := |1 - β| * (MY + Mg)) fun k => ?_
      rw [abs_mul]
      exact mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left ((abs_sub _ _).trans (add_le_add (hMY _ _) (hMg _ _)))
        (abs_nonneg _)
    have sQ : Summable Q := by
      refine summable_geom_bdd hβ0' hβ1 (M := |β * σ| * (Mi + Mπ)) fun k => ?_
      rw [abs_mul]
      exact mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left ((abs_sub _ _).trans (add_le_add (hMi _ _) (hMπ _ _)))
        (abs_nonneg _)
    have e1 : demandSeries β σ Y g i infl t ω = ∑' k, P k - ∑' k, Q k := by
      rw [← sP.tsum_sub sQ]
      refine tsum_congr fun k => ?_
      simp only [hP, hQ]
      ring
    have e2 : β * Bs t ω = ∑' k, P (k + 1) - ∑' k, Q k := by
      rw [← ((summable_nat_add_iff 1).mpr sP).tsum_sub sQ, hBs, ← tsum_mul_left]
      refine tsum_congr fun k => ?_
      simp only [hP, hQ]
      rw [show t + (k + 1) = t + k + 1 by omega, pow_succ]
      ring
    rw [sP.tsum_eq_zero_add] at e1
    have e3 : P 0 = (1 - β) * (Y t ω - g t ω) := by simp [hP]
    simp only [Pi.add_apply, Pi.smul_apply, Pi.sub_apply, smul_eq_mul]
    linarith
  -- hence `Ê_t B_t = Ŷ_t − g_t`
  have hEB : ∀ t, Ehat t (Bs t) = Y t - g t := by
    intro t
    have h1 := hout t
    rw [hsplit, map_add, map_smul, map_smul, hknown] at h1
    have h2 : β • (Ehat t (Bs t) - (Y t - g t)) = 0 := by
      rw [smul_sub]
      funext ω
      have := congrFun h1 ω
      simp only [Pi.add_apply, Pi.smul_apply, Pi.sub_apply, smul_eq_mul, Pi.zero_apply] at this ⊢
      linarith
    exact sub_eq_zero.mp ((smul_eq_zero.mp h2).resolve_left hβ0.ne')
  -- (b) the gap series is `B_t` plus the natural-rate series
  have hgap : ∀ t, (fun ω => ∑' k, β ^ k * ((1 - β) * (fun t => Y t - Yn t) (t + k + 1) ω -
      σ * (i (t + k) ω - infl (t + k + 1) ω - rn (t + k) ω))) =
      Bs t + natSeries β σ g Yn rn t := by
    intro t
    funext ω
    simp only [hBs, natSeries, Pi.add_apply, Pi.sub_apply]
    rw [← (summable_geom_bdd hβ0' hβ1 (bnd1 t ω)).tsum_add
      (summable_geom_bdd hβ0' hβ1 (bnd2 t ω))]
    refine tsum_congr fun k => ?_
    ring
  unfold PrestonIS
  refine forall_congr' fun t => ?_
  rw [hgap, map_add, hEB]
  constructor
  · intro h
    funext ω
    have := congrFun h ω
    simp only [Pi.sub_apply, Pi.add_apply] at this ⊢
    linarith
  · intro h
    rw [h]
    funext ω
    simp only [Pi.sub_apply, Pi.add_apply]
    ring

/-- Woodford (2003), (1.15) and p. 273: **under rational expectations the natural-rate
assumption holds automatically**: if `σ r̂ⁿ_t = h_t − E_t h_{t+1}` with `h = g − Ŷⁿ` bounded and
adapted, then `E_t ∑ β^{T−t}[(1 − β)h_{T+1} + σ r̂ⁿ_T] = h_t` (any `ExpectationSystem`). -/
theorem natSeries_rational {β σ : ℝ} (hβ0 : 0 ≤ β) (hβ1 : β < 1) {g Yn rn : ℕ → Ω → ℝ}
    (hg : BoundedProc g) (hYn : BoundedProc Yn) (ha : 𝔼.Adapted fun t => g t - Yn t)
    (hrn : ∀ t, σ • rn t = (g t - Yn t) - 𝔼.E t (g (t + 1) - Yn (t + 1))) (t : ℕ) :
    𝔼.E t (natSeries β σ g Yn rn t) = g t - Yn t := by
  obtain ⟨Mg, hMg⟩ := hg
  obtain ⟨Mn, hMn⟩ := hYn
  set h : ℕ → Ω → ℝ := fun t => g t - Yn t with hh
  have hb : ∀ t ω, |h t ω| ≤ Mg + Mn := fun t ω =>
    (abs_sub _ _).trans (add_le_add (hMg _ _) (hMn _ _))
  -- the summand as a random variable
  set f : ℕ → Ω → ℝ := fun k => (1 - β) • h (t + k + 1) + (h (t + k) -
    𝔼.E (t + k) (h (t + k + 1))) with hf
  have hfeq : ∀ k ω, (1 - β) * (g (t + k + 1) ω - Yn (t + k + 1) ω) + σ * rn (t + k) ω =
      f k ω := by
    intro k ω
    have := congrFun (hrn (t + k)) ω
    simp only [Pi.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul, Pi.sub_apply] at this
    simp only [hf, hh, Pi.add_apply, Pi.smul_apply, Pi.sub_apply, smul_eq_mul, this]
  have hfb : ∀ k ω, |β ^ k * f k ω| ≤ β ^ k * (|1 - β| * (Mg + Mn) + 2 * (Mg + Mn)) := by
    intro k ω
    rw [abs_mul, abs_pow, abs_of_nonneg hβ0]
    refine mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left ?_ (pow_nonneg hβ0 k)
    simp only [hf, Pi.add_apply, Pi.smul_apply, Pi.sub_apply, smul_eq_mul]
    refine (abs_add_le _ _).trans (add_le_add ?_ ?_)
    · rw [abs_mul]; exact mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left (hb _ _) (abs_nonneg _)
    · refine (abs_sub _ _).trans ?_
      have := 𝔼.abs_E_le (hb (t + k + 1)) (t + k) ω
      linarith [hb (t + k) ω]
  funext ω
  have hser : natSeries β σ g Yn rn t = fun ω => ∑' k, β ^ k * f k ω := by
    funext ω'
    simp only [natSeries, hfeq]
  rw [hser, 𝔼.E_tsum hβ0 hβ1 hfb t ω]
  have hterm : ∀ k, 𝔼.E t (fun ω' => β ^ k * f k ω') ω =
      β ^ k * (𝔼.E t (h (t + k)) ω - β * 𝔼.E t (h (t + (k + 1))) ω) := by
    intro k
    rw [show t + (k + 1) = t + k + 1 by omega]
    have : (fun ω' => β ^ k * f k ω') = β ^ k • f k := by funext ω'; simp
    rw [this, map_smul, hf]
    simp only [map_add, map_sub, map_smul, 𝔼.tower (Nat.le_add_right t k), Pi.smul_apply,
      Pi.add_apply, Pi.sub_apply, smul_eq_mul]
    ring
  simp only [hterm]
  have := tsum_telescope_geom hβ0 hβ1 (a := fun k => 𝔼.E t (h (t + k)) ω)
    (M := Mg + Mn) fun k => 𝔼.abs_E_le (hb _) t ω
  simp only [add_zero] at this
  rw [this, ha t]

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 273: under rational expectations the output form implies the gap form
(2.29) (bounded processes, `Ŷ − g` and `g − Ŷⁿ` adapted, `r̂ⁿ` defined by (1.15)). -/
theorem gapIS_of_rational {β σ : ℝ} (hβ0 : 0 < β) (hβ1 : β < 1) {Y g Yn i infl rn : ℕ → Ω → ℝ}
    (hY : BoundedProc Y) (hg : BoundedProc g) (hYn : BoundedProc Yn) (hi : BoundedProc i)
    (hπ : BoundedProc infl) (hr : BoundedProc rn) (hout : OutputIS 𝔼.E β σ Y g i infl)
    (hYa : ∀ t, 𝔼.E t (Y t - g t) = Y t - g t) (ha : 𝔼.Adapted fun t => g t - Yn t)
    (hrn : ∀ t, σ • rn t = (g t - Yn t) - 𝔼.E t (g (t + 1) - Yn (t + 1))) :
    PrestonIS 𝔼.E β σ (fun t => Y t - Yn t) infl i rn :=
  (gapIS_iff hβ0 hβ1 𝔼.E hY hg hYn hi hπ hr hout hYa).mpr
    (natSeries_rational 𝔼 hβ0.le hβ1 hg hYn ha hrn)

/-- Woodford (2003), p. 273 (correction): **without the natural-rate assumption the gap form
(2.29) does not follow from the output form.** With one state, zero forecasts (which know
`Ŷ_t − g_t = 0`), `Ŷ = g = 1`, `Ŷⁿ = î = π = 0` and `r̂ⁿ = 0` (consistent with (1.15) under
perfect foresight), the output form holds but (2.29) fails since `x = 1`. -/
theorem gapIS_counterexample :
    OutputIS (fun _ => (0 : (Unit → ℝ) →ₗ[ℝ] (Unit → ℝ))) (1 / 2) 1 (fun _ _ => 1)
        (fun _ _ => 1) (fun _ _ => 0) (fun _ _ => 0) ∧
      (0 : (Unit → ℝ) →ₗ[ℝ] (Unit → ℝ)) ((fun _ => (1 : ℝ)) - fun _ => 1) =
        (fun _ => (1 : ℝ)) - (fun _ => 1) ∧
      (∀ t : ℕ, (1 : ℝ) • (fun _ => (0 : ℝ)) = ((fun _ => (1 : ℝ)) - fun _ => 0) -
        perfectForesight.E t ((fun _ => (1 : ℝ)) - fun _ => 0)) ∧
      ¬ PrestonIS (fun _ => (0 : (Unit → ℝ) →ₗ[ℝ] (Unit → ℝ))) (1 / 2) 1
        (fun _ => (fun _ => (1 : ℝ)) - fun _ => 0) (fun _ _ => 0) (fun _ _ => 0)
        (fun _ _ => 0) := by
  refine ⟨fun t => by funext ω; simp, by simp, fun t => by
    funext ω; simp [perfectForesight], fun h => ?_⟩
  have := congrFun (h 0) ()
  norm_num at this

end Preston

end Woodford.NeoWicksellianFramework.Learning
